    "global index": "MATH_213",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compute\n\\[\\sum_{{n = 1}}^\\infty \\frac{{F_{{n + 1}}{{F_n F_{{n + 2}},\\]where $F_n$ denotes the $n$th Fibonacci number, so $F_0 = 0$ and $F_1 = 1.$\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To compute the sum $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n F_{n+2}}$, we use the fundamental Fibonacci identity $F_{n+2} - F_n = F_{n+1}$.\n\nSubstituting this into the numerator of the general term, we have:\n\\[ \\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n F_{n+2}} = \\frac{F_{n+2} - F_n}{F_n F_{n+2}} = \\frac{F_{n+2}}{F_n F_{n+2}} - \\frac{F_n}{F_n F_{n+2}} = \\frac{1}{F_n} - \\frac{1}{F_{n+2}} \\]\n\nThis is a telescoping series. Let $S_k$ be the $k$-th partial sum:\n\\[ S_k = \\sum_{n=1}^k \\left( \\frac{1}{F_n} - \\frac{1}{F_{n+2}} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{1}{F_1} - \\frac{1}{F_3} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{F_2} - \\frac{1}{F_4} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{F_3} - \\frac{1}{F_5} \\right) + \\dots + \\left( \\frac{1}{F_{k-1}} - \\frac{1}{F_{k+1}} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{F_k} - \\frac{1}{F_{k+2}} \\right) \\]\nMost terms cancel out, leaving:\n\\[ S_k = \\frac{1}{F_1} + \\frac{1}{F_2} - \\frac{1}{F_{k+1}} - \\frac{1}{F_{k+2}} \\]\nGiven $F_1 = 1$ and $F_2 = 1$, we have $S_k = 1 + 1 - \\frac{1}{F_{k+1}} - \\frac{1}{F_{k+2}} = 2 - \\frac{1}{F_{k+1}} - \\frac{1}{F_{k+2}}$.\n\nAs $k \\to \\infty$, $F_k \\to \\infty$, so the terms $\\frac{1}{F_{k+1}}$ and $\\frac{1}{F_{k+2}}$ approach 0. Thus, the sum is $2$.\n\n\\boxed{2}",
