    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve the system of equations:\n1. $\\log_6 (x-y) + \\log_6 (x+y) = 2$\n2. $\\log_y 5x = 2$\n\nFirst, simplify equation (1) using the property $\\log_a A + \\log_a B = \\log_a (AB)$:\n$\\log_6 ((x-y)(x+y)) = 2 \\implies x^2 - y^2 = 6^2 = 36$.\n\nNext, simplify equation (2) using the definition of a logarithm:\n$y^2 = 5x$.\n\nSubstitute $y^2 = 5x$ into the first simplified equation:\n$x^2 - 5x = 36 \\implies x^2 - 5x - 36 = 0$.\nFactoring the quadratic gives $(x - 9)(x + 4) = 0$, so $x = 9$ or $x = -4$.\nSince the arguments of logarithms must be positive ($5x > 0$ and $x+y > 0$), we must have $x > 0$, which leaves $x = 9$.\n\n\\boxed{9}",
