    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the domain of $f(x) = \\frac{2-x}{\\log(2-\\log(x-2))}$, we must satisfy three conditions:\n\n1.  The argument of the inner logarithm must be positive: $x - 2 > 0 \\implies x > 2$.\n2.  The argument of the outer logarithm must be positive: $2 - \\log(x - 2) > 0 \\implies \\log(x - 2) < 2 \\implies x - 2 < 10^2 \\implies x < 102$.\n3.  The denominator must not be zero: $\\log(2 - \\log(x - 2)) \\neq 0 \\implies 2 - \\log(x - 2) \\neq 1 \\implies \\log(x - 2) \\neq 1 \\implies x - 2 \\neq 10 \\implies x \\neq 12$.\n\nCombining these conditions ($2 < x < 102$ and $x \\neq 12$), we obtain the domain in interval notation.\n\n\\boxed{(2, 12) \\cup (12, 102)}",
