    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on the central role that T-helper (CD4^+) cells play in coordinating the adaptive immune response. They secrete cytokines necessary for the activation and proliferation of both cytotoxic T-cells (cell-mediated immunity) and B-cells (humoral immunity). Therefore, their depletion leads to a profound collapse of the specific immune system.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
