    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: I nsulin , interferon, and growth hormone have been successfully manufactured in large quantities by the pharmaceutical industries. Explain the importance of genetic engineering in this process.\n\nOptions: \nA. Genetic engineering facilitates the mass production of these proteins by enhancing the animals' ability to produce them in their milk.\nB. Genetic engineering assists in the development of new pharmaceutical drugs.\nC. Genetic engineering is primarily used for cloning organisms, which increases the yield of insulin, interferon, and growth hormone.\nD. Genetic engineering enables the creation of completely synthetic substitutes for insulin, interferon, and growth hormone that do not rely on biological processes.\nE. Genetic engineering improves the nutritional value of food which indirectly helps in the production of these proteins.\nF. Genetic engineering allows for the direct extraction of insulin, interferon, and growth hormone from genetically modified plants.\nG. Genetic engineering is used to modify the human genome to produce insulin, interferon, and growth hormone naturally in the body.\nH. Genetic engineering allows for the large scale production of proteins such as insulin, interferon, and growth hormone through recombinant DNA techniques, lowering their prices and making them more accessible.\nI. Genetic engineering helps in understanding the genetic basis of diseases.\nJ. Genetic engineering aids in the diagnosis of diseases.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
