    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A competitive inhibitor of an enzyme exerts its effect by\n\nOptions: \nA. reversibly modifying some of the amino acid residues that help to comprise the enzyme's active site\nB. irreversibly forming covalent links with the enzyme, effectively preventing the enzyme's dissociation from it\nC. irreversibly modifying some of the amino acid residues that help to comprise the enzyme's active site\nD. reversibly increasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nE. irreversibly decreasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nF. competing with the product molecule for the same enzyme but a different binding site than the product binding site\nG. competing with the substrate molecule for the same enzyme but a different binding site than the substrate binding site\nH. irreversibly forming covalent links with the substrate, effectively preventing the enzyme's dissociation from it\nI. reversibly decreasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nJ. competing with the substrate molecule for the same enzyme and the same binding site as the substrate binding site\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
