    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability, we calculate the probability of each event occurring in sequence:\n\n1.  **First draw (Face card):** There are 12 face cards (Jack, Queen, King of each suit) in a standard deck of 52 cards. The probability is $12/52 = 3/13$.\n2.  **Second draw (Ace):** Since the first card was not replaced, there are 51 cards remaining, 4 of which are Aces. The probability is $4/51$.\n3.  **Combined probability:** Multiply the two probabilities together: $\\frac{3}{13} \\times \\frac{4}{51} = \\frac{12}{663}$.\n\nSimplifying the fraction by dividing both the numerator and denominator by 3 gives $\\frac{4}{221}$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
