    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability of getting exactly three heads in five flips of a balanced coin, we use the binomial probability formula: $P(X=k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$. Here, $n=5$, $k=3$, and $p=0.5$, so the calculation is $\\binom{5}{3} (0.5)^5 = 10 \\times 0.03125 = 0.3125$. Converting this to a percentage gives 31.25%.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
