    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3279",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If X has a normal distribution with mean 9 and standard deviation 3, find P(5 < X < 11).\n\nOptions: \nA. - .09176\nB. .21185\nC. .37748\nD. .55962\nE. .65361\nF. .09176\nG. .92715\nH. .47568\nI. .81743\nJ. .74537\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $P(5 < X < 11)$ for a normal distribution with $\\mu = 9$ and $\\sigma = 3$, we first convert the X-values to Z-scores using the formula $Z = \\frac{X - \\mu}{\\sigma}$.\n\nFor $X = 5$: $Z_1 = \\frac{5 - 9}{3} = \\frac{-4}{3} \\approx -1.33$\nFor $X = 11$: $Z_2 = \\frac{11 - 9}{3} = \\frac{2}{3} \\approx 0.67$\n\nUsing the standard normal distribution table:\n$P(Z < 0.67) \\approx 0.7486$\n$P(Z < -1.33) \\approx 0.0918$\n$P(-1.33 < Z < 0.67) = 0.7486 - 0.0918 = 0.6568$\n\nLooking at the provided options, Option E (.65361) is the closest value resulting from more precise Z-score calculations (using $P(Z < 0.6667) - P(Z < -1.3333)$).\n\n\\boxed{E}",
