    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability that a randomly selected observation is between 50 and 55, we first calculate the z-score for the value 55.\nThe z-score formula is $z = \\frac{x - \\mu}{\\sigma}$, so $z = \\frac{55 - 50}{10} = 0.5$.\nUsing a standard normal distribution table, the area between the mean ($z=0$) and $z=0.5$ is approximately $0.1915$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
