    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3049",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Miniature poodles are thought to have a mean height of 12 inches and a standard deviation of 1.8 inches. If height is measured to the nearest inch, find the percentage of poodles having a height exceeding 14 inches.\n\nOptions: \nA. 45 percent\nB. 2.5 percent\nC. 5 percent\nD. 30 percent\nE. 20 percent\nF. 10 percent\nG. 15 percent\nH. 35 percent\nI. 40 percent\nJ. 25 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the percentage of poodles exceeding 14 inches, we first calculate the z-score for a height of 14 inches. Using the formula $z = (X - \\mu) / \\sigma$, we get $z = (14 - 12) / 1.8 = 2 / 1.8 \\approx 1.11$.\n\nLooking up a z-score of 1.11 in a standard normal distribution table, the area to the left is approximately 0.8665, meaning the area to the right (exceeding 14 inches) is $1 - 0.8665 = 0.1335$, or approximately 13.35%. Among the given options, 15 percent is the closest estimate.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
