    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the popular nursery rhyme \"Mary Had a Little Lamb\", her lambwould follow Mary wherever she went. Discuss a possi-blebiological explanation.\n\nOptions: \nA. The lamb had a habitual path that coincidentally aligned with Mary's route\nB. The lamb might have imprinted on Mary, a form of learning where the lamb forms a strong and lasting bond with the first moving object it sees.\nC. The lamb was guided by a shepherd and instructed to follow Mary\nD. The lamb was genetically programmed to follow Mary\nE. The lamb followed Mary due to a magnetic device she carried\nF. The lamb was trained to follow Mary\nG. The lamb followed Mary because of a distinctive sound she made\nH. The lamb was physically attached to Mary\nI. The lamb was attracted to the color of Mary's clothing\nJ. The lamb had been conditioned to follow a specific scent associated with Mary\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
