    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most likely biological explanation for a young animal following a specific individual is imprinting, a phenomenon famously studied by ethologists like Konrad Lorenz. This process occurs during a critical period shortly after birth, causing the animal to form a strong social attachment to its primary caregiver or the first moving object it encounters.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
