    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4244",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the magnetic moment of 205Tl?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.600 x 10^-26 J T-1\nB. [ɣ (205TI = 1.569 x 108 T-1 s-1, I = ½]\nC. 1.433 x 10^-26 J T-1\nD. 0.717 x 10^-26 J T-1\nE. 0.922 x 10^-26 J T-1\nF. 1.569 x 10^-26 J T-1\nG. 0.750 x 10^-26 J T-1\nH. 1.256 x 10^-26 J T-1\nI. 1.100 x 10^-26 J T-1\nJ. 0.827 x 10^-26 J T-1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the magnetic moment ($\\mu$) of $^{205}\\text{Tl}$, we use the relationship between the gyromagnetic ratio ($\\gamma$) and the magnetic moment:\n$\\mu = \\gamma \\hbar I$\nGiven:\n$\\gamma = 1.569 \\times 10^8 \\text{ T}^{-1}\\text{s}^{-1}$\n$\\hbar = 1.05457 \\times 10^{-34} \\text{ J s}$\n$I = 1/2$\n\nCalculation:\n$\\mu = (1.569 \\times 10^8) \\times (1.05457 \\times 10^{-34}) \\times (0.5)$\n$\\mu \\approx 8.273 \\times 10^{-27} \\text{ J T}^{-1}$ (which is $0.827 \\times 10^{-26} \\text{ J T}^{-1}$)\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, it matches option J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
