    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the limiting high-temperature molar heat capacity at constant volume (C_V) of a gas-phase diatomic molecule?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4.5R\nB. 2.2R\nC. 1R\nD. 4R\nE. 2R\nF. 2.5R\nG. 5R\nH. 3R\nI. 3.5R\nJ. 1.5R\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the limiting high-temperature molar heat capacity ($C_V$) of a gas-phase diatomic molecule, we consider all active degrees of freedom according to the equipartition theorem:\n1. **Translational**: 3 degrees of freedom ($3 \\times \\frac{1}{2}R = 1.5R$).\n2. **Rotational**: 2 degrees of freedom ($2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}R = 1R$).\n3. **Vibrational**: 2 degrees of freedom (1 for kinetic energy and 1 for potential energy, $2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}R = 1R$).\n\nSumming these gives $C_V = 1.5R + 1R + 1R = 3.5R$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
