    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The maximum number of phases that can coexist in equilibrium for a given number of components is governed by the **Gibbs Phase Rule**: $F = C - P + 2$, where $F$ is the degrees of freedom, $C$ is the number of components, and $P$ is the number of phases. For equilibrium to exist, the degrees of freedom $F$ must be at least zero. Plugging in $C = 3$, we get $0 = 3 - P + 2$, which simplifies to $P = 5$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
