      "generated_answer": "To balance the chemical equation $2\\text{Sr}(\\text{NO}_3)_2 + 3\\text{C} + 2\\text{S} \\rightarrow \\text{Products}$, we must account for all atoms on the reactant side:\n- **Strontium (Sr):** 2 atoms\n- **Nitrogen (N):** $2 \\times 2 = 4$ atoms\n- **Oxygen (O):** $2 \\times (3 \\times 2) = 12$ atoms\n- **Carbon (C):** 3 atoms\n- **Sulfur (S):** 2 atoms\n\nLooking at the products in Option I: $2\\text{SrO} + 2\\text{N}_2 + 3\\text{CO}_2 + 2\\text{SO}_2$:\n- Sr: 2 atoms (matches)\n- N: $2 \\times 2 = 4$ atoms (matches)\n- O: $2(1) + 3(2) + 2(2) = 2 + 6 + 4 = 12$ atoms (matches)\n- C: 3 atoms (matches)\n- S: 2 atoms (matches)\n\nThe equation is perfectly balanced with these products.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
