    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve the equation $x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0$ using the quadratic formula $x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$:\n1. Identify the coefficients: $a = 1, b = -5, c = 6$.\n2. Substitute these into the formula: $x = \\frac{5 \\pm \\sqrt{(-5)^2 - 4(1)(6)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{5 \\pm \\sqrt{25 - 24}}{2} = \\frac{5 \\pm 1}{2}$.\n3. Calculate the two possible values: $x = \\frac{6}{2} = 3$ and $x = \\frac{4}{2} = 2$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
