    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3367",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate the percentage difference between $\\ln (1+x)$ and $x$ for $x=0.0050$\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.490 %\nB. 3.750 %\nC. 0.005 %\nD. 0.050 %\nE. 4.990 %\nF. 1.250 %\nG. 5.000 %\nH. 0.100 %\nI. 0.025 %\nJ.  0.249 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the percentage difference between $\\ln(1+x)$ and $x$, we use the Taylor series expansion for $\\ln(1+x) = x - \\frac{x^2}{2} + \\frac{x^3}{3} - \\dots$\n\nThe difference is approximately $x - \\ln(1+x) \\approx \\frac{x^2}{2}$.\nThe percentage difference is calculated as:\n$\\text{Percentage Difference} = \\frac{x - \\ln(1+x)}{x} \\times 100\\% \\approx \\frac{x^2/2}{x} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{x}{2} \\times 100\\%$.\n\nSubstituting $x = 0.0050$:\n$\\frac{0.0050}{2} \\times 100\\% = 0.0025 \\times 100\\% = 0.25\\%$.\n\nLooking at the options, $0.249\\%$ (Option J) is the closest value, accounting for the slight underestimation by ignoring higher-order terms of the series.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
