      "generated_answer": "To find the orbital angular momentum quantum number ($l$) of the electron most easily removed from ground-state aluminum (Al), we first determine its electron configuration. Aluminum has an atomic number of 13, so its ground-state configuration is $[Ne] 3s^2 3p^1$. The electron most easily removed is the outermost valence electron, which resides in the $3p$ orbital. For a $p$ orbital, the orbital angular momentum quantum number $l$ is equal to 1.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
