    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3567",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Solve 6x^2 - 7x - 20 = 0.\n\nOptions: \nA. 5/2, 4/3\nB. -5/3, 4/2\nC. 5/3, -4/2\nD. 2, -10\nE. 4, -5\nF. -5/2, 4/3\nG. -5/6, 4/5\nH. 5/2, -4/3\nI. 5, 4\nJ. 5, -4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve the quadratic equation $6x^2 - 7x - 20 = 0$, we can use the quadratic formula $x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$:\n\n1.  Identify the coefficients: $a = 6$, $b = -7$, and $c = -20$.\n2.  Calculate the discriminant: $b^2 - 4ac = (-7)^2 - 4(6)(-20) = 49 + 480 = 529$.\n3.  Find the roots: $x = \\frac{7 \\pm \\sqrt{529}}{12} = \\frac{7 \\pm 23}{12}$.\n    *   $x_1 = \\frac{7 + 23}{12} = \\frac{30}{12} = \\frac{5}{2}$\n    *   $x_2 = \\frac{7 - 23}{12} = \\frac{-16}{12} = -\\frac{4}{3}$\n\nComparing these results to the options, they match option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
