    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The overall rate of a chemical reaction is determined by the slowest step, known as the rate-determining step. For the proposed mechanism, the slow step is $\\text{NO}_2 + \\text{F}_2 \\rightarrow \\text{NO}_2\\text{F} + \\text{F}$, which leads to the rate law: $\\text{Rate} = k[\\text{NO}_2]^1[\\text{F}_2]^1$. The overall order is the sum of the exponents in the rate law ($1 + 1 = 2$).\n\n\\boxed{B}",
