      "generated_answer": "The correct interpretation of a confidence interval refers to the probability that the true population parameter (in this case, the mean income per family of all students in the school) falls within the calculated range. \n\n*   Options A, E, and J are incorrect because they describe the distribution of individual data points, not the population mean.\n*   Options B and C are incorrect as they describe the behavior of future intervals rather than the current one.\n*   Option D correctly identifies that the 95% confidence level expresses our uncertainty regarding the location of the true population mean.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
