    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the value of the product of the partial derivatives, we use the implicit function theorem for a surface defined by $F(x, y, z) = 0$.\n\nAssuming $x, y, z$ are mutually dependent variables, the partial derivatives are given by:\n$\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial y} = -\\frac{F_y}{F_x}$, $\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial z} = -\\frac{F_z}{F_y}$, and $\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial x} = -\\frac{F_x}{F_z}$.\n\nMultiplying these together:\n$\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial y} \\cdot \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial z} \\cdot \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial x} = \\left(-\\frac{F_y}{F_x}\\right) \\left(-\\frac{F_z}{F_y}\\right) \\left(-\\frac{F_x}{F_z}\\right) = (-1)^3 \\frac{F_y F_z F_x}{F_x F_y F_z} = -1$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
