  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6504",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the sum of $\\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} (1/e^n + 1/(n*(n+1)))$\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.234\nB. 1.414\nC. 2.000\nD. 1.581\nE. 2.718\nF. 1.618\nG. 1.789\nH. 1.000\nI. 3.141\nJ. 2.345\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the sum of the series $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac{1}{e^n} + \\frac{1}{n(n+1)}\\right)$, we can split it into two separate convergent series:\n\n1.  **The geometric series:** $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{e^n} = \\frac{1/e}{1 - 1/e} = \\frac{1}{e-1}$.\n    Using $e \\approx 2.71828$, we get $\\frac{1}{1.71828} \\approx 0.58197$.\n2.  **The telescoping series:** $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n(n+1)} = \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac{1}{n} - \\frac{1}{n+1}\\right) = (1 - \\frac{1}{2}) + (\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3}) + \\dots = 1$.\n\nAdding the two results together: $0.58197 + 1 = 1.58197$. This matches option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
