    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find $\\int_{{0}}^{{\\sqrt{{3}} \\frac{{dx}}{{1+x^2}}$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.0944\nB. 1.7321\nC. 1.0472\nD. 2.4495\nE. 2.3562\nF. 0.7854\nG. 1.5708\nH. 3.1416\nI. 0.9553\nJ. 0.5236\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the value of the integral $\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\frac{dx}{1+x^2}$, we use the standard integration formula $\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2} dx = \\arctan(x)$.\n\n1. Evaluate the antiderivative at the boundaries: $[\\arctan(x)]_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}$.\n2. Calculate the values: $\\arctan(\\sqrt{3}) - \\arctan(0) = \\frac{\\pi}{3} - 0 = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n3. Using the approximation $\\pi \\approx 3.14159$, we get $\\frac{3.14159}{3} \\approx 1.047197$.\n\nComparing this to the options, $1.0472$ corresponds to choice C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
