    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7484",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For every positive real number $x$, let $g(x)=\\lim _{{r \\rightarrow 0}}((x+1)^{{r+1}}-x^{{r+1}})^{{1/r}}$. What is the limit of $g(x)/x$ as $x$ goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. Infinity\nC. 3.1415926\nD. 1\nE. 0\nF. 1.6180339\nG. 1.4142135\nH. 1.7320508\nI. 2.7182818\nJ. 3.1415927\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $g(x)$, we evaluate the limit $g(x) = \\lim_{r \\to 0} ((x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1})^{1/r}$.\nLet $f(r) = (x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1}$. As $r \\to 0$, $f(r) \\to (x+1) - x = 1$.\nThe limit is of the form $1^{1/0}$, which is an indeterminate form $1^\\infty$. We use the identity $\\lim_{r \\to 0} a^{1/r} = e^{\\lim_{r \\to 0} \\frac{\\ln(a)}{r}}$.\nApplying this to $g(x)$:\n$\\ln(g(x)) = \\lim_{r \\to 0} \\frac{\\ln((x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1})}{r}$.\nUsing L'Hôpital's Rule with respect to $r$:\n$\\frac{d}{dr} \\ln((x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1}) = \\frac{(x+1)^{r+1} \\ln(x+1) - x^{r+1} \\ln x}{(x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1}}$.\nEvaluating at $r=0$: $\\frac{(x+1) \\ln(x+1) - x \\ln x}{(x+1) - x} = (x+1) \\ln(x+1) - x \\ln x$.\nThus, $g(x) = e^{(x+1) \\ln(x+1) - x \\ln x}$.\nWe want the limit of $\\frac{g(x)}{x}$ as $x \\to \\infty$.\n$g(x) = e^{\\ln((x+1)^{x+1}) - \\ln(x^x)} = \\frac{(x+1)^{x+1}}{x^x} = \\frac{(x+1)^x (x+1)}{x^x} = (1 + \\frac{1}{x})^x (x+1)$.\nAs $x \\to \\infty$, $(1 + \\frac{1}{x})^x \\to e$.\nSo, $g(x) \\approx e(x+1)$.\nThen $\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\frac{g(x)}{x} = \\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\frac{e(x+1)}{x} = e \\approx 2.7182818$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
