    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7472",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sum the series $\\sum_{{m=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}}\\frac{{m^2 n}}{{3^m(n3^m+m3^n)}}$\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.23456\nB. 0.41567\nC. 0.19375\nD. 0.28125\nE. 0.62500\nF. 0.14659\nG. 0.51234\nH. 0.33333\nI. 0.73145\nJ. 0.77777\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve the series $S = \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{m^2 n}{3^m(n 3^m + m 3^n)}$, we can utilize the symmetry of the expression. Let the general term be $a_{m,n} = \\frac{m^2 n}{3^m(n 3^m + m 3^n)}$.\n\nConsider the term $a_{n,m} = \\frac{n^2 m}{3^n(m 3^n + n 3^m)}$.\nObserve that:\n$a_{m,n} + a_{n,m} = \\frac{m^2 n}{3^m(n 3^m + m 3^n)} + \\frac{n^2 m}{3^n(m 3^n + n 3^m)} = \\frac{m^2 n \\cdot 3^n + n^2 m \\cdot 3^m}{3^m 3^n (n 3^m + m 3^n)} = \\frac{mn(m 3^n + n 3^m)}{3^{m+n}(n 3^m + m 3^n)} = \\frac{mn}{3^{m+n}}$.\n\nBy symmetry, $2S = \\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{mn}{3^{m+n}} = \\left(\\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{m}{3^m}\\right) \\left(\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{n}{3^n}\\right)$.\nThe sum of the arithmetico-geometric series $\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} k x^k = \\frac{x}{(1-x)^2}$. For $x = \\frac{1}{3}$, this sum is $\\frac{1/3}{(2/3)^2} = \\frac{1/3}{4/9} = \\frac{3}{4}$.\nThus, $2S = \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{9}{16}$, which means $S = \\frac{9}{32} = 0.28125$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
