  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7249",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the sum of $\\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} (cost(1/n^2) - cost(1/(n+1)^2))$\n\nOptions: \nA. -2.459\nB. -1.459\nC. -0.159\nD. 2.459\nE. 0.959\nF. 0.159\nG. 1.000\nH. 0.459\nI. 1.459\nJ. -0.459\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the sum of the series $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} (\\cos(1/n^2) - \\cos(1/(n+1)^2))$, we recognize it as a **telescoping series**.\n\nThe sum of the first $k$ terms is:\n$S_k = (\\cos(1/1^2) - \\cos(1/2^2)) + (\\cos(1/2^2) - \\cos(1/3^2)) + \\dots + (\\cos(1/k^2) - \\cos(1/(k+1)^2))$\n$S_k = \\cos(1) - \\cos(1/(k+1)^2)$\n\nAs $n \\to \\infty$, the term $1/(n+1)^2 \\to 0$, and $\\cos(0) = 1$. Therefore:\n$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} (\\cos(1/n^2) - \\cos(1/(n+1)^2)) = \\cos(1) - 1$\n\nUsing the value $\\cos(1) \\approx 0.5403$:\n$0.5403 - 1 = -0.4597$\n\nThis value most closely matches option J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
