    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7207",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let I != A != -I, where I is the identity matrix and A is a real 2 x 2 matrix. If A = A^(-1), then the trace of A is\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.5\nB. 0\nC. 3\nD. 1\nE. -2\nF. 2\nG. -4\nH. 4\nI. -3\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the trace of the matrix $A$, we start with the given condition $A = A^{-1}$. This implies $A^2 = I$, meaning $A$ is an involutory matrix.\n\nThe eigenvalues $\\lambda$ of an involutory matrix must satisfy $\\lambda^2 = 1$, so $\\lambda \\in \\{1, -1\\}$. For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, there are three possibilities for the pair of eigenvalues:\n1. $\\lambda_1 = 1, \\lambda_2 = 1 \\implies A = I$ (Excluded by the condition $A \\neq I$).\n2. $\\lambda_1 = -1, \\lambda_2 = -1 \\implies A = -I$ (Excluded by the condition $A \\neq -I$).\n3. $\\lambda_1 = 1, \\lambda_2 = -1$.\n\nThe trace of a matrix is the sum of its eigenvalues. In the only remaining case, $\\text{tr}(A) = 1 + (-1) = 0$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
