      "generated_answer": "To find $K_f$ (the kernel of the homomorphism $f$), we identify the elements in the domain $U_5$ that map to the identity element of the codomain $U_5$. \n\n1. The group $U_5$ (the multiplicative group of integers modulo 5) consists of the set $\\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}$.\n2. The identity element of $U_5$ is $1$.\n3. We solve $f(x) = x^2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}$ for $x \\in \\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}$:\n   - $1^2 = 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}$ (Solution)\n   - $2^2 = 4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}$\n   - $3^2 = 9 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}$\n   - $4^2 = 16 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}$ (Solution)\n\nThe kernel $K_f$ is the set $\\{1, 4\\}$. Looking at the options, this corresponds to the pair $[4, 1]$ or $[1, 4]$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
