    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7266",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the fundamental period of the given function:\n$$f(x)=\\left\\{{\\begin{{array}}{{ll}}(-1)^n, & 2 n-1 \\leq x<2 n, \\\\ 1, & 2 n \\leq x<2 n+1 ;\\end{{array}} \\quad n=0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2, \\ldots\\right.$$\n\nOptions: \nA. √2 (the square root of 2)\nB. 2\nC. 5\nD. 3\nE. π (pi)\nF. 1\nG. 6\nH. 2.5\nI. 8\nJ.  4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the fundamental period of the function $f(x)$, let's analyze its values over a range of $x$:\n- For $n=0$: $x \\in [-1, 0) \\implies f(x) = (-1)^0 = 1$; $x \\in [0, 1) \\implies f(x) = 1$.\n- For $n=1$: $x \\in [1, 2) \\implies f(x) = (-1)^1 = -1$; $x \\in [2, 3) \\implies f(x) = 1$.\n- For $n=2$: $x \\in [3, 4) \\implies f(x) = (-1)^2 = 1$; $x \\in [4, 5) \\implies f(x) = 1$.\n- For $n=3$: $x \\in [5, 6) \\implies f(x) = (-1)^3 = -1$; $x \\in [6, 7) \\implies f(x) = 1$.\n\nObserving the pattern, the values of $f(x)$ are:\n$x \\in [0, 1): 1$\n$x \\in [1, 2): -1$\n$x \\in [2, 3): 1$\n$x \\in [3, 4): 1$\n$x \\in [4, 5): 1$\n$x \\in [5, 6): -1$\n$x \\in [6, 7): 1$\n$x \\in [7, 8): 1$\n\nThe pattern of values is $(1, -1, 1, 1)$ repeating every 4 units (e.g., $f(x)$ on $[0, 4)$ is $1$ on $[0, 1)$, $-1$ on $[1, 2)$, $1$ on $[2, 3)$, and $1$ on $[3, 4)$; this repeats for $[4, 8)$). Thus, $f(x+4) = f(x)$, and the fundamental period is 4.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
