    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the domain of $h(x) = \\sqrt{25-x^2} + \\sqrt{-(x-2)}$, we must ensure the expressions under the square roots are non-negative:\n1. $25 - x^2 \\geq 0 \\implies x^2 \\leq 25 \\implies -5 \\leq x \\leq 5$.\n2. $-(x - 2) \\geq 0 \\implies x - 2 \\leq 0 \\implies x \\leq 2$.\n\nThe intersection of these two intervals is $[-5, 5] \\cap (-\\infty, 2] = [-5, 2]$.\nThe width of this interval is $2 - (-5) = 7$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
