    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6719",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: for the matrix $A=(\\begin{{array}}{{rrrrr}} 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & -3 \\1 & 2 & 0 & -5 & 1 \\2 & 4 & -3 & -19 & 6 \\3 & 6 & -3 & -24 & 7\\end{{array}})$, what is its row rank and column rank? return the two numbers as a list.\n\nOptions: \nA. [1, 1]\nB. [3, 4]\nC. [4, 4]\nD. [2, 4]\nE. [2, 3]\nF. [3, 3]\nG. [4, 2]\nH. [2, 2]\nI. [4, 3]\nJ. [3, 2]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the rank of matrix $A$, we perform Gaussian elimination to reach the row-echelon form:\n1.  $R_2 \\to R_2 - R_1$, $R_3 \\to R_3 - 2R_1$, $R_4 \\to R_4 - 3R_1$ gives:\n    $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -27 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -12 & -36 & 16 \\end{pmatrix}$\n2.  Observe that $R_3 = 3R_2$ and $R_4 = 4R_2$.\n3.  Subtracting $3R_2$ from $R_3$ and $4R_2$ from $R_4$ results in two zero rows, leaving two non-zero rows.\n\nSince the row rank is 2, and the row rank always equals the column rank for any matrix, both are 2.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
