  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7446",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When the graph of a certain function $f(x)$ is shifted $2$ units to the right and stretched vertically by a factor of $2$ (meaning that all $y$-coordinates are doubled), the resulting figure is identical to the original graph. Given that $f(0)=0.1$, what is $f(10)$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.01\nB. 32\nC. 3.2\nD. 5\nE. 1\nF. 0.2\nG. 0.5\nH. 2\nI. 10\nJ. 20\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the relationship for $f(x)$, we translate the given transformations into an equation. Shifting $f(x)$ 2 units to the right gives $f(x-2)$, and stretching it vertically by a factor of 2 gives $2f(x-2)$. Since the resulting figure is identical to the original, we have:\n$$f(x) = 2f(x-2)$$\nTo find $f(10)$ given $f(0) = 0.1$, we apply this recursive relationship:\n$f(2) = 2f(0) = 2(0.1)$\n$f(4) = 2f(2) = 2^2(0.1)$\n$f(6) = 2f(4) = 2^3(0.1)$\n$f(8) = 2f(6) = 2^4(0.1)$\n$f(10) = 2f(8) = 2^5(0.1) = 32 \\times 0.1 = 3.2$\n\nComparing this result to the options, $3.2$ corresponds to choice C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
