    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6912",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the greatest common divisor of $2^{{1001}}-1$ and $2^{{1012}}-1$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1024\nB. 2049\nC. 2048\nD. 4096\nE. 2\nF. 4095\nG. 1\nH. 511\nI. 2047\nJ. 2050\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers of the form $2^a - 1$ and $2^b - 1$, we use the property:\n$\\gcd(2^a - 1, 2^b - 1) = 2^{\\gcd(a, b)} - 1$.\n\nIn this problem, $a = 1001$ and $b = 1012$.\nFirst, find the GCD of the exponents:\n$\\gcd(1001, 1012) = \\gcd(1001, 1012 - 1001) = \\gcd(1001, 11)$.\nSince $1001 = 11 \\times 91$, the $\\gcd(1001, 1012) = 11$.\n\nApplying the property:\n$\\gcd(2^{1001} - 1, 2^{1012} - 1) = 2^{11} - 1 = 2048 - 1 = 2047$.\n\nComparing this result to the options:\nI. 2047\n\n\\boxed{I}",
