    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7436",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The maximum number of acute angles in a convex 10-gon in the Euclidean plane is\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 2\nC. 7\nD. 9\nE. 4\nF. 6\nG. 1\nH. 5\nI. 8\nJ. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the maximum number of acute angles in a convex $n$-gon, we consider the sum of the exterior angles. For any convex polygon, the sum of the exterior angles is always $360^\\circ$. \n\nAn interior angle is acute (less than $90^\\circ$) if and only if its corresponding exterior angle is obtuse (greater than $90^\\circ$). Since the sum of exterior angles is $360^\\circ$, there can be at most three obtuse exterior angles (because four obtuse angles would sum to more than $4 \\times 90^\\circ = 360^\\circ$). Therefore, a convex polygon of any number of sides $n \\ge 3$ can have at most 3 acute interior angles.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
