  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7277",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A small kiosk at the Atlanta airport carries souvenirs in the price range of $3.99 to $29.99, with a mean price of $14.75. The airport authorities decide to increase the rent charged for a kiosk by 5 percent. To make up for the increased rent, the kiosk owner decides to increase the prices of all items by 50 cents. As a result, which of the following will happen?\n\nOptions: \nA. The range and standard deviation of prices will increase by 50 cents, but the mean price will remain the same.\nB. The standard deviation of prices will increase by 50 cents, but the mean price and the range will remain the same.\nC. The mean price will increase by 50 cents, but the standard deviation of prices will remain the same.\nD. The mean price will remain the same, but the standard deviation of prices will increase by 50 cents.\nE. The mean price and the range of prices will increase by 50 cents.\nF. The mean price and the standard deviation of prices will increase by 50 cents.\nG. The mean price will remain the same, but the range of prices will increase by 50 cents.\nH. The mean price will increase by 50 cents, but the range of prices will decrease by 50 cents.\nI. The mean price, the range, and the standard deviation of prices will all remain the same.\nJ. The range of prices will increase by 50 cents, but the mean price and the standard deviation will remain the same.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the effect of adding a constant value (50 cents) to every data point in a set, we apply the basic properties of measures of center and spread:\n\n1.  **Mean:** Adding a constant $c$ to every value in a data set increases the mean by that constant. Thus, the mean price increases from $\\$14.75$ to $\\$15.25$.\n2.  **Range:** The range is the difference between the maximum and minimum values. Since both the maximum ($\\$29.99 + 0.50$) and the minimum ($\\$3.99 + 0.50$) increase by the same amount, the difference remains exactly the same.\n3.  **Standard Deviation:** Standard deviation measures the dispersion of data points relative to the mean. Because every point and the mean shift by the same amount, the distance between the points and the mean does not change, and the standard deviation remains constant.\n\nTherefore, the mean increases by 50 cents, while the range and standard deviation remain the same.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
