    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6892",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If $f(x)=ax^6-bx^4+x-1$ and $f(2)=5$, then what is the value of $f(-2)$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 1\nC. 2\nD. 0\nE. -5\nF. -2\nG. 5\nH. -3\nI. -1\nJ. 3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the value of $f(-2)$, we examine the structure of the function $f(x) = ax^6 - bx^4 + x - 1$.\n\n1. Notice that the terms $ax^6$ and $-bx^4$ are even functions (the exponents are even), meaning $ax^6$ and $-bx^4$ yield the same value for $x$ and $-x$.\n2. Let $g(x) = ax^6 - bx^4 - 1$. This is an even function, so $g(2) = g(-2)$.\n3. We can write $f(x) = g(x) + x$.\n   - $f(2) = g(2) + 2 = 5 \\implies g(2) = 3$.\n   - $f(-2) = g(-2) + (-2) = g(2) - 2 = 3 - 2 = 1$.\n\nThe value of $f(-2)$ is 1.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
