    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the statements:\n1. **Statement 1:** A free abelian group is isomorphic to a direct sum of copies of $\\mathbb{Z}$. Since $\\mathbb{Z}$ is torsion-free and the direct sum of torsion-free groups is torsion-free, every free abelian group is torsion-free. This statement is **True**.\n2. **Statement 2:** According to the Fundamental Theorem of Finitely Generated Abelian Groups, any finitely generated abelian group $G$ is isomorphic to $\\mathbb{Z}^r \\oplus \\mathbb{Z}_{n_1} \\oplus \\dots \\oplus \\mathbb{Z}_{n_k}$. If $G$ is torsion-free, the torsion part ($\\mathbb{Z}_{n_i}$) must be zero, leaving $G \\cong \\mathbb{Z}^r$, which is a free abelian group. This statement is **True**.\n\nSince both statements are true, the correct option is I.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
