    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6649",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose X and Y are random variables with E(X) = 312, var(X) = 6, E(X) = 307, and var(Y) = 8. What are the expected value and variance of the random variable X + Y?\n\nOptions: \nA. E(X + Y) = 307, var(X + Y) = 10\nB. E(X + Y) = 307, var(X + Y) = 6\nC. E(X + Y) = 619, var(X + Y) = 14\nD. E(X + Y) = 619, var(X + Y) = 7\nE. E(X + Y) = 312, var(X + Y) = 14\nF. E(X + Y) = 312, var(X + Y) = 8\nG. There is insufficient information to answer this question.\nH. E(X + Y) = 619, var(X + Y) = 8\nI. E(X + Y) = 619, var(X + Y) = 6\nJ. E(X + Y) = 619, var(X + Y) = 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the expected value and variance of the sum of two random variables $X$ and $Y$:\n\n1.  **Expected Value**: By the linearity of expectation, $E(X + Y) = E(X) + E(Y)$. Using the values provided (assuming the second \"E(X)\" in the prompt was meant to be $E(Y)$), $E(X + Y) = 312 + 307 = 619$.\n2.  **Variance**: If $X$ and $Y$ are assumed to be independent (which is the standard assumption for these types of multiple-choice questions when no covariance is provided), $\\text{var}(X + Y) = \\text{var}(X) + \\text{var}(Y)$. Thus, $\\text{var}(X + Y) = 6 + 8 = 14$.\n3.  Comparing these results to the options, $E(X + Y) = 619$ and $\\text{var}(X + Y) = 14$ matches Option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
