  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7645",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let f(x, y) = x^3 + y^3 + 3xy for all real x and y. Then there exist distinct points P and Q such that f has a\n\nOptions: \nA. local maximum at P and a saddle point at Q\nB. local minimum at P and at Q\nC. local minimum at P and a local maximum at Q\nD. saddle point at P and a local minimum at Q\nE. saddle point at P and a local maximum at Q\nF. no distinct points P and Q where f has a local maximum or saddle point\nG. local minimum at P and a saddle point at Q\nH. local maximum at P and at Q\nI. local maximum at P and a local minimum at Q\nJ. saddle point at P and at Q\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the critical points of $f(x, y) = x^3 + y^3 + 3xy$, we calculate the first partial derivatives and set them to zero:\n$f_x = 3x^2 + 3y = 0 \\implies y = -x^2$\n$f_y = 3y^2 + 3x = 0 \\implies x = -y^2$\nSubstituting $y = -x^2$ into the second equation gives $x = -(-x^2)^2 = -x^4$, so $x(1 + x^3) = 0$. The real solutions are $x = 0$ (which gives $y = 0$) and $x = -1$ (which gives $y = -1$). Thus, the critical points are $P(0, 0)$ and $Q(-1, -1)$.\n\nNext, we use the second derivative test. The Hessian matrix is $H = \\begin{pmatrix} f_{xx} & f_{xy} \\\\ f_{yx} & f_{yy} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6x & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6y \\end{pmatrix}$.\nThe determinant is $D(x, y) = 36xy - 9$.\n1. At $P(0, 0)$: $D(0, 0) = -9$. Since $D < 0$, $P$ is a **saddle point**.\n2. At $Q(-1, -1)$: $D(-1, -1) = 36(-1)(-1) - 9 = 27$. Since $D > 0$ and $f_{xx}(-1, -1) = -6 < 0$, $Q$ is a **local maximum**.\n\nThus, there exist distinct points $P$ (saddle point) and $Q$ (local maximum).\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 240,
        "output_tokens": 427,
        "total_tokens": 667
      },
