$f(x) = (x-1)x(x+1)$, no.\nIf $f(x) = x(x+1)^2$, $f(99) = 99(100^2) = 990000$. This is Option I.\nFor this matrix $A$, the eigenvalues are $0, 0, -1, -2$ is not it.\nThe characteristic polynomial is $x^2(x+1)(x-1)$? No.\n$p(x) = x^2(x+1)(x-2)$? $\\text{Tr} = 1$.\n$p(x) = x^2(x+2)(x-1)$? $\\text{Tr} = -1$.\nActually, $f(x) = x^2(x+1)$ would give $99^2 \\times 100 = 980100$.\n$f(x) = x(x+1)^2$ would give $99 \\times 100^2 = 990000$.\nThe minimal polynomial for this specific matrix is $f(x) = x(x+1)^2$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
