    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the sum of all integer solutions to $|n| < |n-3| < 9$?\n\nOptions: \nA. -9\nB. -4\nC. 0\nD. 9\nE. 4\nF. -14\nG. 19\nH. -19\nI. 14\nJ. -24\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the sum of all integer solutions to $|n| < |n-3| < 9$, we break the inequality into two parts:\n\n1.  **$|n| < |n-3|$**: Squaring both sides gives $n^2 < (n-3)^2$, which simplifies to $n^2 < n^2 - 6n + 9$. This results in $6n < 9$, or $n < 1.5$.\n2.  **$|n-3| < 9$**: This means $-9 < n-3 < 9$, which simplifies to $-6 < n < 12$.\n\nCombining these, we need integers $n$ such that $-6 < n < 1.5$. The integer solutions are $\\{-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1\\}$. Summing these values: $-5 + (-4) + (-3) + (-2) + (-1) + 0 + 1 = -14$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
