    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7252",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suppose a,b,c,\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma are six real numbers with a^2+b^2+c^2>0.  In addition, $a=b*cos(\\gamma)+c*cos(\\beta), b=c*cos(\\alpha)+a*cos(\\gamma), c=a*cos(\\beta)+b*cos(\\alpha)$. What is the value of $cos^2(\\alpha)+cos^2(\\beta)+cos^2(\\gamma)+2*cos(\\alpha)*cos(\\beta)*cos(\\gamma)? return the numeric.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.5\nB. 0.0\nC. 2.0\nD. 1.0\nE. -0.5\nF. 1.5\nG. -1.0\nH. 2.5\nI. 3.0\nJ. 0.25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given equations are:\n1) $a = b\\cos\\gamma + c\\cos\\beta$\n2) $b = c\\cos\\alpha + a\\cos\\gamma$\n3) $c = a\\cos\\beta + b\\cos\\alpha$\n\nThis is a system of linear equations for $a, b, c$ which can be written as:\n$\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -\\cos\\gamma & -\\cos\\beta \\\\ -\\cos\\gamma & 1 & -\\cos\\alpha \\\\ -\\cos\\beta & -\\cos\\alpha & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$\n\nFor a non-trivial solution to exist (since $a^2+b^2+c^2 > 0$), the determinant of the matrix must be zero:\n$\\det = 1(1 - \\cos^2\\alpha) + \\cos\\gamma(-\\cos\\gamma - \\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta) - \\cos\\beta(\\cos\\gamma\\cos\\alpha + \\cos\\beta) = 0$\n$1 - \\cos^2\\alpha - \\cos^2\\gamma - \\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma - \\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma - \\cos^2\\beta = 0$\n$1 - (\\cos^2\\alpha + \\cos^2\\beta + \\cos^2\\gamma + 2\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma) = 0$\nTherefore, $\\cos^2\\alpha + \\cos^2\\beta + \\cos^2\\gamma + 2\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta\\cos\\gamma = 1$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
