    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6692",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the smallest positive integer $n$ such that $\\frac{{1}}{{n}}$ is a terminating decimal and $n$ contains the digit 9?\n\nOptions: \nA. 512\nB. 1024\nC. 128\nD. 72\nE. 32\nF. 256\nG. 2048\nH. 64\nI. 8192\nJ. 4096\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine if a fraction $\\frac{1}{n}$ is a terminating decimal, the prime factorization of $n$ must be of the form $2^a \\cdot 5^b$, where $a, b$ are non-negative integers.\n\nWe check the provided options to see which satisfy this condition and contain the digit 9:\n- A. 512 ($2^9$) - No digit 9.\n- B. 1024 ($2^{10}$) - No digit 9.\n- C. 128 ($2^7$) - No digit 9.\n- D. 72 ($2^3 \\cdot 3^2$) - Not a terminating decimal.\n- E. 32 ($2^5$) - No digit 9.\n- F. 256 ($2^8$) - No digit 9.\n- G. 2048 ($2^{11}$) - No digit 9.\n- H. 64 ($2^6$) - No digit 9.\n- I. 8192 ($2^{13}$) - Contains digit 9 and is a power of 2.\n- J. 4096 ($2^{12}$) - Contains digit 9 and is a power of 2.\n\nComparing the candidates that contain the digit 9 and result in terminating decimals, 4096 is smaller than 8192.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
