    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6952",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the value of the inflection point of f(x) =(10 ln(x))/(x^2)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.000\nB. 1.587\nC. 0.693\nD. 1.203\nE. 3.014\nF. 2.718\nG. 4.000\nH. 3.142\nI. 1.000\nJ. 2.301\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inflection point of $f(x) = \\frac{10 \\ln(x)}{x^2}$, we must find where the second derivative $f''(x) = 0$.\n\n1.  **First Derivative**: Using the quotient rule, $f'(x) = 10 \\cdot \\frac{(1/x)(x^2) - (2x)(\\ln x)}{x^4} = 10 \\cdot \\frac{x - 2x \\ln x}{x^4} = \\frac{10(1 - 2 \\ln x)}{x^3}$.\n2.  **Second Derivative**: Applying the quotient rule again, $f''(x) = 10 \\cdot \\frac{(-2/x)(x^3) - (3x^2)(1 - 2 \\ln x)}{x^6} = 10 \\cdot \\frac{-2x^2 - 3x^2 + 6x^2 \\ln x}{x^6} = \\frac{10(6 \\ln x - 5)}{x^4}$.\n3.  **Solve for $x$**: Setting $f''(x) = 0$ gives $6 \\ln x - 5 = 0$, so $\\ln x = \\frac{5}{6}$.\n4.  **Calculate Value**: $x = e^{5/6} \\approx 2.30097$.\n\nComparing this to the options, $2.301$ is the closest value.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
