    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6816",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: V is a vector space over the real field R. It is known that the vector group u_1, u_2, u_3 in V are linearly independent. Finding the rank of vector group ${{u_1-\\lambda u_2, u_2-\\lambda u_3, u_3-\\lambda u_1}}$ for $\\lambda=\\sqrt{{5}}$ and $\\lambda=1$ separately. Return the answer as a list.\n\nOptions: \nA. [1, 2]\nB. [2, 1]\nC. [3, 2]\nD. [1, 1]\nE. [2, 3]\nF. [3, 1]\nG. [3, 3]\nH. [1, 3]\nI. [2, 2]\nJ. [0, 2]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the rank of the vector group $\\{u_1-\\lambda u_2, u_2-\\lambda u_3, u_3-\\lambda u_1\\}$, we represent the vectors as a linear combination of the linearly independent basis $\\{u_1, u_2, u_3\\}$. The coefficients form the matrix:\n$$A = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -\\lambda & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\lambda \\\\ -\\lambda & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$$\nThe rank of the vector group is equal to the rank of this matrix. The determinant is $\\det(A) = 1(1) - (-\\lambda)(0 - \\lambda^2) + 0 = 1 - \\lambda^3$.\n\n1. For $\\lambda = \\sqrt{5}$, $\\det(A) = 1 - (\\sqrt{5})^3 = 1 - 5\\sqrt{5} \\neq 0$. Since the determinant is non-zero, the rank is 3.\n2. For $\\lambda = 1$, $\\det(A) = 1 - 1^3 = 0$. The matrix becomes $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$. The first two rows are linearly independent, but the third row is the negative sum of the first two ($R_3 = -R_1 - R_2$), so the rank is 2.\n\nThe ranks are [3, 2].\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
