    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the possible values of $g(25)$, we set $f(x) = 25$ and solve for $x$.\n$3x^2 - 2 = 25 \\implies 3x^2 = 27 \\implies x^2 = 9 \\implies x = 3$ or $x = -3$.\n\nUsing the given composite function $g(f(x)) = x^2 + x + 1$:\n1. For $x = 3$: $g(25) = (3)^2 + 3 + 1 = 9 + 3 + 1 = 13$.\n2. For $x = -3$: $g(25) = (-3)^2 + (-3) + 1 = 9 - 3 + 1 = 7$.\n\nThe sum of all possible values of $g(25)$ is $13 + 7 = 20$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
