      "generated_answer": "**Statement 1 is False.** The degree of the sum of two polynomials is less than or equal to the maximum of their degrees ($\\deg(f+g) \\leq \\max(\\deg f, \\deg g)$); it can be strictly less if the leading terms cancel each other out (e.g., $f(x) = x^2$ and $g(x) = -x^2 + 1$).\n\n**Statement 2 is True.** Since $F$ is a field, $F[x]$ is a Principal Ideal Domain (PID), meaning every ideal in $F[x]$ is generated by a single element.\n\nComparing these results to the options, Statement 1 is False and Statement 2 is True.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
