    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7699",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| Every group of order p^2 where p is prime is Abelian. Statement 2 | For a fixed prime p a Sylow p-subgroup of a group G is a normal subgroup of G if and only if it is the only Sylow p-subgroup of G.\n\nOptions: \nA. Statement 1 is true for certain prime numbers, Statement 2 is true for certain prime numbers\nB. Both statements are true only for certain prime numbers\nC. Statement 1 is false, Statement 2 is true only for certain prime numbers\nD. Statement 1 is true, Statement 2 is false for certain prime numbers\nE. True, True\nF. False, True\nG. Statement 1 is true only for certain prime numbers, Statement 2 is false\nH. Statement 1 is false for certain prime numbers, Statement 2 is true\nI. False, False\nJ. True, False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the statements:\n\n**Statement 1:** This is a standard result in group theory. Every group of order $p^2$ (where $p$ is prime) is isomorphic to either $\\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ or $\\mathbb{Z}_p \\times \\mathbb{Z}_p$, both of which are Abelian. Thus, Statement 1 is **True**.\n\n**Statement 2:** According to Sylow's Theorems, all Sylow $p$-subgroups are conjugate to one another. A subgroup is normal if and only if it is equal to all its conjugates; therefore, a Sylow $p$-subgroup is normal if and only if it is unique. Thus, Statement 2 is **True**.\n\nSince both statements are true for all primes $p$, the correct option is \"True, True\".\n\n\\boxed{E}",
