    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_7887",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the value of (I / I_0) for the first diagonal maximum of the Fraunhoferdiffraction pattern of a circular aperture.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.145\nB. 0.215\nC. 0.155\nD. 0.125\nE. 0.175\nF. 0.165\nG. 0.185\nH. 0.235\nI. 0.205\nJ. 0.195\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The intensity distribution for the Fraunhofer diffraction pattern of a circular aperture is given by the Airy disk formula:\n$I = I_0 \\left( \\frac{2J_1(ka\\sin\\theta)}{ka\\sin\\theta} \\right)^2$\nwhere $J_1$ is the Bessel function of the first kind of order one. The first maximum (the first side lobe) occurs at the first local maximum of the function $\\frac{J_1(x)}{x}$, which happens at $x \\approx 5.1356$. Substituting this value into the intensity formula:\n$I/I_0 = \\left( \\frac{2J_1(5.1356)}{5.1356} \\right)^2 \\approx (0.4027)^2 \\approx 0.162$ or more precisely $0.1622$.\n\nAmong the given options, 0.165 is the closest standard approximation used in many textbook contexts for the first side-maximum.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
