    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_9027",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The dirt floor of theShanidarCave in the northern part of Iraq has been examined. Below the layer of soil that contained arrowheads and bone awls was a layer of soil that yielded flint tools and pieces of charcoal. When the charcoal was examined it was discovered that in 1 kg of carbon, approximately 9.4 × 10^2 carbon\\Elzbar14 nuclei decayed each second. It is known that in 1 kg of carbon from living material, 1.5 × 10^4 disintegrations of carbon\\Elzbar14 occur each second. Use these data to calculate when people of the stone age culture occupied the cave.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6.5 × 10^4 years ago\nB. 4.6 × 10^4 years ago\nC. 9.4 × 10^2 years ago\nD. 8.8 × 10^3 years ago\nE. 5730 years ago\nF. 2.3 × 10^4 years ago\nG. 11,460 years ago\nH. 7.3 × 10^3 years ago\nI. 1.5 × 10^4 years ago\nJ. 3.0 × 10^4 years ago\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the age of the charcoal, we use the radioactive decay formula:\n$N = N_0 e^{-\\lambda t}$ or $A = A_0 e^{-\\lambda t}$, where $A$ is the current activity, $A_0$ is the initial activity, and $\\lambda$ is the decay constant.\n\n1.  **Identify the values:**\n    $A = 9.4 \\times 10^2 \\text{ disintegrations/s}$\n    $A_0 = 1.5 \\times 10^4 \\text{ disintegrations/s}$\n    Half-life of $^{14}\\text{C} \\approx 5730 \\text{ years}$\n    $\\lambda = \\frac{\\ln(2)}{5730} \\approx 1.2097 \\times 10^{-4} \\text{ year}^{-1}$\n\n2.  **Calculate the time ($t$):**\n    $\\frac{A}{A_0} = e^{-\\lambda t} \\implies \\ln\\left(\\frac{9.4 \\times 10^2}{1.5 \\times 10^4}\\right) = -\\lambda t$\n    $\\ln(0.062667) = -1.2097 \\times 10^{-4} \\times t$\n    $-2.770 = -1.2097 \\times 10^{-4} \\times t$\n    $t = \\frac{2.770}{1.2097 \\times 10^{-4}} \\approx 22,900 \\text{ years}$\n\nComparing this result to the options, it most closely matches $2.3 \\times 10^4$ years.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
