  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_9018",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The interior of a refrigerator is typically held at $36^{{\\circ}} \\mathrm{{F}}$ and the interior of a freezer is typically held at $0.00^{{\\circ}} \\mathrm{{F}}$. If the room temperature is $65^{{\\circ}} \\mathrm{{F}}$, by what factor is it more expensive to extract the same amount of heat from the freezer than from the refrigerator? Assume that the theoretical limit for the performance of a reversible refrigerator is valid in this case.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.2\nB. 2.0\nC. 1.2\nD. 2.7\nE. 3.5\nF.  2.4\nG. 4.0\nH. 1.5\nI. 5.0\nJ. 1.8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the relative expense of extracting heat, we use the coefficient of performance (COP) for a reversible refrigerator: $\\text{COP} = \\frac{T_L}{T_H - T_L}$, where temperatures must be in Kelvin.\n\n1.  **Convert temperatures to Kelvin:**\n    *   Room temperature ($T_H$): $65^\\circ\\text{F} = \\frac{65-32}{1.8} + 273.15 \\approx 291.61\\text{ K}$\n    *   Refrigerator ($T_{L, \\text{ref}}$): $36^\\circ\\text{F} = \\frac{36-32}{1.8} + 273.15 \\approx 275.37\\text{ K}$\n    *   Freezer ($T_{L, \\text{frz}}$): $0^\\circ\\text{F} = \\frac{0-32}{1.8} + 273.15 \\approx 255.37\\text{ K}$\n\n2.  **Calculate the COP for both:**\n    *   $\\text{COP}_{\\text{ref}} = \\frac{275.37}{291.61 - 275.37} = \\frac{275.37}{16.24} \\approx 16.96$\n    *   $\\text{COP}_{\\text{frz}} = \\frac{255.37}{291.61 - 255.37} = \\frac{255.37}{36.24} \\approx 7.05$\n\n3.  **Calculate the factor of expense:**\n    The work required is $W = \\frac{Q}{\\text{COP}}$. The factor by which it is more expensive is the ratio of the work required:\n    $\\text{Factor} = \\frac{W_{\\text{frz}}}{W_{\\text{ref}}} = \\frac{\\text{COP}_{\\text{ref}}}{\\text{COP}_{\\text{frz}}} = \\frac{16.96}{7.05} \\approx 2.40$\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 247,
