    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_7790",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the half-cell reaction $\\operatorname{{AgCl}}(s)+\\mathrm{{e}}^{{-}} \\rightarrow$ $\\operatorname{{Ag}}(s)+\\mathrm{{Cl}}^{{-}}(a q)$. If $\\mu^{{\\circ}}(\\mathrm{{AgCl}}, s)=-109.71 \\mathrm{{~kJ}} \\mathrm{{~mol}}^{{-1}}$, and if $E^{{\\circ}}=+0.222 \\mathrm{{~V}}$ for this half-cell, calculate the standard Gibbs energy of formation of $\\mathrm{{Cl}}^{{-}}(a q)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. -137.5 $\\mathrm{{~kJ}} \\mathrm{{~mol}}^{{-1}}$\nB. -140.9 kJ mol^{{-1}}\nC.  -131.1 $\\mathrm{{~kJ}} \\mathrm{{~mol}}^{{-1}}$\nD. -145.2 $\\mathrm{{~kJ}} \\mathrm{{~mol}}^{{-1}}$\nE. -122.7 $\\mathrm{{~kJ}} \\mathrm{{~mol}}^{{-1}}$\nF. -128.4 kJ mol^{{-1}}\nG. -155.7 kJ mol^{{-1}}\nH. -150.3 kJ mol^{{-1}}\nI. -100.0 kJ mol^{{-1}}\nJ. -115.6 kJ mol^{{-1}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the standard Gibbs energy of formation of $\\text{Cl}^- (aq)$, we use the relationship between the standard cell potential ($E^\\circ$) and the standard Gibbs energy change ($\\Delta G^\\circ$) for the half-cell reaction:\n$$\\Delta G^\\circ = -nFE^\\circ$$\nGiven $n = 1$, $F = 96485 \\text{ C mol}^{-1}$, and $E^\\circ = +0.222 \\text{ V}$:\n$$\\Delta G^\\circ = -(1)(96485)(0.222) \\approx -21419.7 \\text{ J mol}^{-1} = -21.42 \\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$$\nThe reaction is $\\text{AgCl}(s) + \\text{e}^- \\rightarrow \\text{Ag}(s) + \\text{Cl}^-(aq)$. The energy change is:\n$$\\Delta G^\\circ = \\mu^\\circ(\\text{Ag}, s) + \\mu^\\circ(\\text{Cl}^-, aq) - \\mu^\\circ(\\text{AgCl}, s)$$\nStandard Gibbs energy of formation for an element in its stable state is zero ($\\mu^\\circ(\\text{Ag}, s) = 0$).\n$$-21.42 = 0 + \\mu^\\circ(\\text{Cl}^-, aq) - (-109.71)$$\n$$\\mu^\\circ(\\text{Cl}^-, aq) = -21.42 - 109.71 = -131.13 \\text{ kJ mol}^{-1}$$\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, it matches Option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
