    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8448",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which configuration of battery and resistors will create a circuit with the greatest current?\n\nOptions: \nA. A high voltage battery with resistors arranged in parallel\nB. A high voltage battery with resistors arranged in series\nC. A low voltage battery with resistors arranged in parallel\nD. Multiple low voltage batteries with resistors arranged in series\nE. A low voltage battery with resistors arranged in series\nF. A medium voltage battery with resistors arranged in parallel\nG. A medium voltage battery with resistors arranged in series\nH. A low voltage battery with no resistors\nI. Multiple high voltage batteries with resistors arranged in parallel\nJ. A high voltage battery with no resistors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "According to Ohm's Law ($I = V/R$), the current ($I$) is maximized when the voltage ($V$) is at its highest and the resistance ($R$) is at its lowest. A high voltage battery provides the maximum potential difference, while the absence of resistors minimizes the resistance to nearly zero (ideally). Therefore, a high voltage battery with no resistors will produce the greatest current.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
