    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if a card is drawn from a well shuffled pack of cards , the probability of drawing a spade or a king is - .\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 / 10\nB. 4 / 13\nC. 3 / 5\nD. 9 / 7\nE. 1 / 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability of drawing a spade or a king, we use the formula for the union of two events: $P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B)$.\n\n1.  There are 13 spades in a deck of 52 cards: $P(\\text{Spade}) = 13/52$.\n2.  There are 4 kings in a deck: $P(\\text{King}) = 4/52$.\n3.  There is 1 card that is both a spade and a king (the King of Spades): $P(\\text{Spade} \\cap \\text{King}) = 1/52$.\n4.  Calculation: $(13/52) + (4/52) - (1/52) = 16/52$.\n5.  Simplifying the fraction: $16/52 = 4/13$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
