    "global index": "MathQA_1412",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 55 cubic centimetres of silver is drawn into a wire 1 mm in diameter . the length of the wire in metres will be :\n\nOptions: \nA. 84 m\nB. 88 m\nC. 120 m\nD. 70 m\nE. none\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the length of the wire, we use the formula for the volume of a cylinder: $V = \\pi r^2 h$.\n\n1.  **Given values:** Volume $V = 55\\text{ cm}^3$; Diameter $= 1\\text{ mm}$, so radius $r = 0.5\\text{ mm} = 0.05\\text{ cm}$.\n2.  **Calculation:** $55 = \\frac{22}{7} \\times (0.05)^2 \\times h \\implies 55 = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 0.0025 \\times h$.\n3.  **Solving for $h$:** $h = \\frac{55 \\times 7}{22 \\times 0.0025} = \\frac{385}{0.055} = 7000\\text{ cm}$.\n4.  **Convert to metres:** $7000\\text{ cm} = 70\\text{ m}$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
