    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: on a ranch , a rancher can place a loop of rope , called a lasso , once in every 3 throws around a cow ’ s neck . what is the probability that the rancher will be able to place a lasso around a cow ’ s neck at least once in 3 attempts ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 3\nB. 5 / 9\nC. 7 / 9\nD. 19 / 27\nE. 23 / 27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability of at least one success in 3 attempts, it is easiest to calculate the complement: the probability of failing in all 3 attempts.\n\n1. The probability of success on a single throw is $1/3$, so the probability of failure is $1 - 1/3 = 2/3$.\n2. The probability of failing 3 times in a row is $(2/3)^3 = 8/27$.\n3. The probability of at least one success is $1 - 8/27 = 19/27$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
