    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if x is a number such that x ^ 2 + 2 x - 24 = 0 and x ^ 2 - 5 x + 4 = 0 , then x =\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. - 4\nC. - 3\nD. - 6\nE. 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the value of $x$, we solve both quadratic equations and look for the common root.\n\n1.  Solving $x^2 + 2x - 24 = 0$:\n    Factoring gives $(x + 6)(x - 4) = 0$, so $x = -6$ or $x = 4$.\n2.  Solving $x^2 - 5x + 4 = 0$:\n    Factoring gives $(x - 4)(x - 1) = 0$, so $x = 4$ or $x = 1$.\n\nThe only value of $x$ that satisfies both equations is 4.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
