    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the required amount of concentrate, first calculate the total volume of juice needed: $240 \\text{ servings} \\times 6 \\text{ ounces/serving} = 1,440 \\text{ ounces}$. \n\nSince the ratio is 1 part concentrate to 3 parts water, there are 4 total parts of liquid. One part (the concentrate) is $1,440 \\div 4 = 360 \\text{ ounces}$.\n\nFinally, divide the total concentrate needed by the size of one can: $360 \\text{ ounces} \\div 12 \\text{ ounces/can} = 30 \\text{ cans}$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
