    "global index": "MathQA_1714",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: this year , mbb consulting fired 6 % of its employees and left remaining employee salaries unchanged . sally , a first - year post - mba consultant , noticed that that the average ( arithmetic mean ) of employee salaries at mbb was 10 % more after the employee headcount reduction than before . the total salary pool allocated to employees after headcount reduction is what percent of that before the headcount reduction ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 98.5 %\nB. 100.0 %\nC. 102.8 %\nD. 103.4 %\nE. 105.0 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the total salary pool after the reduction, we use the formula for the average salary: $\\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Total Salary Pool}}{\\text{Number of Employees}}$.\n\n1. Let $N$ be the initial number of employees and $S$ be the initial total salary pool. Initial average = $S/N$.\n2. After the reduction, the number of employees is $0.94N$ and the average salary is $1.10 \\times (S/N)$.\n3. The new total salary pool is $\\text{New Average} \\times \\text{New Headcount} = (1.10 \\times S/N) \\times 0.94N = 1.10 \\times 0.94 \\times S = 1.034S$.\n\nThe new total salary pool is $103.4\\%$ of the original pool.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
