    "global index": "MathQA_2482",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: what is the range of all the roots of | x ^ 2 - 3 | = x ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 3\nC. 2\nD. 1\nE. 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the range of the roots, we solve the equation $|x^2 - 3| = x$ by considering two cases: $x^2 - 3 = x$ and $x^2 - 3 = -x$.\n1. For $x^2 - x - 3 = 0$, the roots are $x = \\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}$; since $x$ must be non-negative, we take $x_1 = \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} \\approx 2.30$.\n2. For $x^2 + x - 3 = 0$, the roots are $x = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}$; taking the non-negative value gives $x_2 = \\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} \\approx 1.30$.\nThe range is the difference between the largest and smallest roots: $x_1 - x_2 = \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} - \\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
