  {
    "global index": "MathQA_128",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: rani bought more apples than oranges . she sells apples at ₹ 23 apiece and makes 15 % profit . she sells oranges at ₹ 10 apiece and makes 25 % profit . if she gets ₹ 653 after selling all the apples and oranges , find her profit percentage z .\n\nOptions: \nA. 16.8 %\nB. 17.4 %\nC. 17.9 %\nD. 18.5 %\nE. 19.1 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the profit percentage, we need to determine the number of apples ($a$) and oranges ($o$) sold.\nGiven the total revenue: $23a + 10o = 653$.\nSince $a$ and $o$ must be integers and $a > o$, we test values for $a$:\nIf $a = 21$, $10o = 653 - 483 = 170 \\Rightarrow o = 17$ (Satisfies $a > o$).\nIf $a = 11$, $10o = 653 - 253 = 400 \\Rightarrow o = 40$ (Does not satisfy $a > o$).\n\nNow, calculate the total cost price (CP):\n$\\text{CP of apples} = \\frac{23 \\times 21}{1.15} = \\frac{483}{1.15} = 420$\n$\\text{CP of oranges} = \\frac{10 \\times 17}{1.25} = \\frac{170}{1.25} = 136$\n$\\text{Total CP} = 420 + 136 = 556$\n\nTotal Profit = $\\text{Total Revenue} - \\text{Total CP} = 653 - 556 = 97$\n$\\text{Profit Percentage } z = \\left(\\frac{97}{556}\\right) \\times 100 \\approx 17.446\\%$\n\nComparing this to the options, 17.4% is the closest match.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 184,
        "output_tokens": 377,
