    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a 12 meter long wire is cut into two pieces . if the longer piece is then used to form a perimeter of a square , what is the probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 if the original wire was cut at an arbitrary point ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 6\nB. 2 / 3\nC. 3 / 10\nD. 1 / 3\nE. 2 / 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability, let the cut be made at a point $x$ (where $0 \\le x \\le 12$). The length of the longer piece $L$ will be $\\max(x, 12-x)$.\nThe perimeter of the square is $L$, so the side length is $L/4$ and the area is $(L/4)^2$.\nWe want the area to be greater than 4:\n$(L/4)^2 > 4 \\implies L/4 > 2 \\implies L > 8$.\nThe longer piece $L$ is greater than 8 if $x > 8$ or $12-x > 8$ (which means $x < 4$).\nThe total length of the intervals where $x < 4$ or $x > 8$ is $4 + 4 = 8$ units.\nThe probability is the length of the favorable region divided by the total length: $8/12 = 2/3$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
