    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the distance between $P$ and $Q$, let the distance from $R$ to $Q$ be $x$.\n1. According to the problem, $S$ is a point between $R$ and $Q$ such that $RS = SQ$. Since the distance $RS = 50\\text{ km}$, the distance $RQ = RS + SQ = 50 + 50 = 100\\text{ km}$.\n2. The distance $PR$ is half the distance $RQ$, so $PR = 100 / 2 = 50\\text{ km}$.\n3. The total distance $PQ = PR + RQ = 50 + 100 = 150\\text{ km}$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
