    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Hardware-enforced control-flow integrity (CFI), such as Intel's Control-flow Enforcement Technology (CET), utilizes a shadow version of this structure to prevent Return-Oriented Programming (ROP) attacks. This mechanism stores a copy of return addresses in a protected memory area to ensure they are not overwritten by buffer overflows. Upon a return instruction, the CPU compares the address on the data stack with the one on the shadow version to verify integrity.\n\n\\boxed{stack}",
