  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10043",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a bridge hand of 13 cards, what is the probability of (a) having neither an ace nor a king, (b) having no ace or one ace and exactly four kings. Assume that the random variables X and Y represent the number of aces and kings respectively. Also assume that (^52 _13) possible bridge hands are equally likely.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.0810, 0.0020\nB. 0.0799, 0.0019\nC. 0.0830, 0.0016\nD. 0.0808, 0.0023\nE. 0.0820, 0.0021\nF. 0.0822, 0.0018\nG. 0.0818, 0.0022\nH. 0.0812, 0.0024\nI. 0.0825, 0.0017\nJ. 0.0805, 0.0025\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve for the probabilities, we use the hypergeometric distribution formula: $P(X=x, Y=y) = \\frac{\\binom{4}{x} \\binom{4}{y} \\binom{44}{13-x-y}}{\\binom{52}{13}}$.\n\n(a) For neither an ace nor a king ($X=0, Y=0$):\n$P(0,0) = \\frac{\\binom{4}{0} \\binom{4}{0} \\binom{44}{13}}{\\binom{52}{13}} = \\frac{44! / (13! 31!)}{52! / (13! 39!)} = \\frac{44 \\cdot 43 \\cdots 32}{52 \\cdot 51 \\cdots 40} \\approx 0.0818$.\n\n(b) For no ace ($X=0$) or one ace ($X=1$) and exactly four kings ($Y=4$):\n$P(X=0, Y=4) = \\frac{\\binom{4}{0} \\binom{4}{4} \\binom{44}{9}}{\\binom{52}{13}} \\approx 0.00117$\n$P(X=1, Y=4) = \\frac{\\binom{4}{1} \\binom{4}{4} \\binom{44}{8}}{\\binom{52}{13}} \\approx 0.00103$\nTotal probability = $0.00117 + 0.00103 \\approx 0.0022$.\n\nComparing these results to the options, they match Option G.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 329,
        "output_tokens": 388,
        "total_tokens": 717
      },
      "provider": "openai",
