    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The variance of the sum of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula:\n$\\text{Var}(X + Y) = \\text{Var}(X) + \\text{Var}(Y) + 2\\text{Cov}(X, Y)$.\n\nThe covariance $\\text{Cov}(X, Y)$ is defined as the expected value of the product of the deviations of $X$ and $Y$ from their means:\n$\\text{Cov}(X, Y) = E[(X - E(X))(Y - E(Y))]$.\n\nSubstituting this into the variance formula gives $\\text{Var}(Z) = \\text{Var}(X) + \\text{Var}(Y) + 2E[(X - E(X))(Y - E(Y))]$, which matches option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
