    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10313",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Obtain the partial-fraction expansion of F(s) = [(s + 2) / {{(s + 1)^2 (s + 3)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. F(s) = [(1 / 5) / (s + 1)] + [(2 / 5) / (s + 1)^2] - [(2 / 5) / (s + 3)]\nB. F(s) = [(1 / 2) / (s + 1)] - [(1 / 2) / (s + 1)^2] + [(1 / 4) / (s + 3)]\nC. F(s) = [(3 / 4) / (s + 1)] - [(1 / 8) / (s + 1)^2] - [(5 / 8) / (s + 3)]\nD. F(s) = [(1 / 2) / (s + 1)^2] + [(1 / 4) / (s + 1)] - [(1 / 4) / (s + 3)]\nE. F(s) = [(1 / 6) / (s + 1)] + [(1 / 3) / (s + 1)^2] - [(1 / 2) / (s + 3)]\nF. F(s) = [(1 / 2) / (s + 1)] + [(1 / 4) / (s + 1)] + [(1 / 4) / (s + 3)]\nG. F(s) = [(1 / 2) / (s + 1)] + [(1 / 4) / (s + 1)^2] - [(1 / 4) / (s + 3)]\nH. F(s) = [(1 / 3) / (s + 1)] + [(1 / 3) / (s + 1)^2] + [(1 / 3) / (s + 3)]\nI. F(s) = [(1 / 2) / (s + 1)] + [(1 / 6) / (s + 1)^2] + [(1 / 3) / (s + 3)]\nJ. F(s) = [(1 / 2) / (s + 1)^2] + [(1 / 4) / (s + 1)] + [(1 / 4) / (s + 3)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the partial-fraction expansion of $F(s) = \\frac{s + 2}{(s + 1)^2 (s + 3)}$, we set up the form:\n$F(s) = \\frac{A}{s + 1} + \\frac{B}{(s + 1)^2} + \\frac{C}{s + 3}$\n\n1. **Find $B$ (Heaviside cover-up method):**\n$B = \\left. \\frac{s + 2}{s + 3} \\right|_{s = -1} = \\frac{-1 + 2}{-1 + 3} = \\frac{1}{2}$\n\n2. **Find $C$ (Heaviside cover-up method):**\n$C = \\left. \\frac{s + 2}{(s + 1)^2} \\right|_{s = -3} = \\frac{-3 + 2}{(-3 + 1)^2} = \\frac{-1}{4} = -\\frac{1}{4}$\n\n3. **Find $A$:**\nUsing $s = 0$: $F(0) = \\frac{2}{(1)^2(3)} = \\frac{2}{3}$.\n$\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{A}{1} + \\frac{1/2}{1} + \\frac{-1/4}{3} \\implies \\frac{2}{3} = A + \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{12} \\implies \\frac{2}{3} = A + \\frac{5}{12}$.\n$A = \\frac{8}{12} - \\frac{5}{12} = \\frac{3}{12} = \\frac{1}{4}$.\n\nThe expansion is $F(s) = \\frac{1/4}{s + 1} + \\frac{1/2}{(s + 1)^2} - \\frac{1/4}{s + 3}$. This matches option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
