    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10111",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the inverse Laplace transform of F(s), where F(s) is given by F(s) = [(3s + 1) / {{(s - 1)(s^2 + 1)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. 3e^t + sin t - cos t\nB. e^t - cos t + sin t\nC. e^t - sin t - cos t\nD. e^t + cos t - 2 sin t\nE. 3e^t - cos t - 2 sin t\nF. 2e^t + sin t + 2 cos t\nG. 2e^t - 2 cos t + sin t\nH. 2e^t - 2 sin t + cos t\nI. e^t - 2 cos t + 2 sin t\nJ. 2e^t + 2 cos t - sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s) = \\frac{3s + 1}{(s - 1)(s^2 + 1)}$, we use partial fraction decomposition:\n$$\\frac{3s + 1}{(s - 1)(s^2 + 1)} = \\frac{A}{s - 1} + \\frac{Bs + C}{s^2 + 1}$$\nMultiplying by the denominator gives $3s + 1 = A(s^2 + 1) + (Bs + C)(s - 1)$.\nSetting $s = 1$: $3(1) + 1 = A(1^2 + 1) \\implies 4 = 2A \\implies A = 2$.\nComparing coefficients for $s^2$: $0 = A + B \\implies B = -A = -2$.\nComparing constants: $1 = A - C \\implies 1 = 2 - C \\implies C = 1$.\n\nThus, $F(s) = \\frac{2}{s - 1} + \\frac{-2s + 1}{s^2 + 1} = 2\\left(\\frac{1}{s - 1}\\right) - 2\\left(\\frac{s}{s^2 + 1}\\right) + 1\\left(\\frac{1}{s^2 + 1}\\right)$.\nTaking the inverse Laplace transform: $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\{F(s)\\} = 2e^t - 2\\cos t + \\sin t$.\n\nMatching this result with the options, it corresponds to Option G.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
      "success": true,
