  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10334",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A three input information channel with all three input symbols equally probable, is defined by the channel matrix, \\vert0.50.30.2\\vert \\vert0.20.30.5\\vert \\vert0.30.30.4\\vert Assuming that a maximum-likelihood decision rule is used, determine the error probability, P_E, of the channel.\n\nOptions: \nA. (13) / (30)\nB. (19) / (30)\nC. (15) / (30)\nD. (18) / (30)\nE. (14) / (30)\nF. (17) / (30)\nG. (21) / (30)\nH. (12) / (30)\nI. (16) / (30)\nJ. (20) / (30)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the error probability $P_E$, we use the channel matrix $P(y|x)$, where rows represent inputs $x_1, x_2, x_3$ and columns represent outputs $y_1, y_2, y_3$:\n$P = \\begin{pmatrix} 0.5 & 0.3 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.3 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.3 & 0.4 \\end{pmatrix}$\n\nSince all input symbols are equally probable, the Maximum Likelihood (ML) decision rule chooses the input $x_i$ that maximizes $P(y_j|x_i)$ for a given received symbol $y_j$:\n- For $y_1$: $\\max(0.5, 0.2, 0.3) = 0.5$ (choose $x_1$). Correct probability: $0.5$.\n- For $y_2$: $\\max(0.3, 0.3, 0.3) = 0.3$ (tie; choosing any gives the same result). Correct probability: $0.3$.\n- For $y_3$: $\\max(0.2, 0.5, 0.4) = 0.5$ (choose $x_2$). Correct probability: $0.5$.\n\nThe probability of a correct decision $P_C$ is the average of the maximum probabilities weighted by the probability of receiving each $y_j$. Since inputs are equiprobable ($P(x) = 1/3$), the probability of receiving $y_j$ is $P(y_j) = \\frac{1}{3} \\sum_{i} P(y_j|x_i)$:\n- $P(y_1) = \\frac{1}{3}(0.5+0.2+0.3) = 1/3$\n- $P(y_2) = \\frac{1}{3}(0.3+0.3+0.3) = 0.3$\n- $P(y_3) = \\frac{1}{3}(0.2+0.5+0.4) = 1.1/3$\n\n$P_C = \\sum P(y_j) \\cdot P(x_{ML}|y_j) = \\frac{1}{3}(0.5) + \\frac{1}{3}(0.3) + \\frac{1}{3}(0.5) = \\frac{1.3}{3} = \\frac{13}{30}$ (Wait, the formula for $P_C$ is $\\sum_j \\max_i P(y_j|x_i) P(x_i)$ if inputs are equiprobable: $P_C = \\frac{1}{3}(0.5 + 0.3 + 0.5) = \\frac{1.3}{3} = \\frac{13}{30}$).\nHowever, the error probability is $P_E = 1 - P_C = 1 - \\frac{13}{30} = \\frac{17}{30}$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 278,
        "output_tokens": 718,
