  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10721",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the Fourier sine series of f(x) = x^2 over the interval (0, 1).\n\nOptions: \nA. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)]}} sinn\\pix\nB. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{2 / (n\\pi)]}} sinn\\pix\nC. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nD. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)] + [{{4}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nE. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n}} / (n^2\\pi^2)]}} sinn\\pix\nF. x^2 \\sim_s 2 ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)] + [{{2[1 - (- 1)^n]}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nG. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{1}} / (n\\pi)] + [{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n^2\\pi^2)]}} sinn\\pix\nH. x^2 \\sim_s 2 ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{1 / (n^2\\pi^2)}} sinn\\pix\nI. x^2 \\sim_s 2 ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)] - [{{2[1 - (- 1)^n]}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nJ. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n^2\\pi^2)] - [{{2[1 - (- 1)^n]}} / (n^4\\pi^4)]}} sinn\\pix\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the Fourier sine series of $f(x) = x^2$ on $(0, 1)$, we calculate the coefficients $b_n$:\n$b_n = 2 \\int_0^1 x^2 \\sin(n\\pi x) dx$.\nUsing integration by parts twice:\n1. Let $u = x^2, dv = \\sin(n\\pi x)dx \\implies du = 2x dx, v = -\\frac{\\cos(n\\pi x)}{n\\pi}$.\n   $\\int x^2 \\sin(n\\pi x) dx = -\\frac{x^2 \\cos(n\\pi x)}{n\\pi} + \\int \\frac{2x \\cos(n\\pi x)}{n\\pi} dx$.\n2. For the second integral, let $u = 2x, dv = \\cos(n\\pi x)dx \\implies du = 2 dx, v = \\frac{\\sin(n\\pi x)}{n\\pi}$.\n   $\\int \\frac{2x \\cos(n\\pi x)}{n\\pi} dx = \\frac{2x \\sin(n\\pi x)}{n^2\\pi^2} - \\int \\frac{2 \\sin(n\\pi x)}{n^2\\pi^2} dx = \\frac{2x \\sin(n\\pi x)}{n^2\\pi^2} + \\frac{2 \\cos(n\\pi x)}{n^3\\pi^3}$.\n\nEvaluating from 0 to 1:\n$b_n = 2 \\left[ -\\frac{\\cos(n\\pi)}{n\\pi} + 0 + \\frac{2\\cos(n\\pi)}{n^3\\pi^3} - \\frac{2}{n^3\\pi^3} \\right] = 2 \\left[ \\frac{-(-1)^n}{n\\pi} + \\frac{2((-1)^n - 1)}{n^3\\pi^3} \\right]$.\nRewriting this: $b_n = 2 \\left[ \\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi} - \\frac{2(1 - (-1)^n)}{n^3\\pi^3} \\right]$.\n\nComparing this result to the options, it matches Option I.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 591,
        "output_tokens": 520,
