  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10877",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the function, g(x) = (1 + x^2)^-1 Determine a constant k such that f(x) = k(1 + x^2)^-1 is a proper probability density for - \\infty < x < \\infty. Find F(x) = Pr(X \\leq x) if X is distributed with density function f(x).\n\nOptions: \nA. π\nB. 3/π\nC. 1/2π\nD. 1/π^2\nE. π^2\nF. π/2\nG. 2/π\nH. 4/π\nI. 1/π\nJ. 1/2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the constant $k$, we use the property that the total area under a probability density function (PDF) must equal 1:\n$$\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, dx = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\frac{k}{1 + x^2} \\, dx = 1$$\nThe integral of $\\frac{1}{1+x^2}$ is $\\arctan(x)$. Evaluating this from $-\\infty$ to $\\infty$:\n$$k [\\arctan(x)]_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} = k \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\left( -\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right) \\right) = k\\pi = 1$$\nSolving for $k$, we get $k = \\frac{1}{\\pi}$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
