    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 0 - 100 V voltmeter has a guaranteed accuracy of 2 % of full scale reading. The voltage measured by the voltmeter is 75 V. The limiting error is in percentage\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 %.\nB. 2.66 %.\nC. 2.5 %.\nD. 5 %.\nE. 2 %.\nF. 1.5 %.\nG. 2.33 %.\nH. 3.33 %.\nI. 3 %.\nJ. 4 %.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the limiting error (relative error) for the specific measurement, we first calculate the absolute error based on the full-scale reading.\n\n1. **Absolute Error:** The accuracy is 2% of the full scale (100 V), which is $0.02 \\times 100\\text{ V} = 2\\text{ V}$.\n2. **Limiting Error at 75 V:** The relative limiting error is the absolute error divided by the actual measured value:\n   $$\\text{Limiting Error} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Absolute Error}}{\\text{Measured Value}} \\right) \\times 100 = \\left( \\frac{2\\text{ V}}{75\\text{ V}} \\right) \\times 100 \\approx 2.666...\\%$$\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, 2.66% is the closest match.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
