    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the determinant $\\Delta = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -2 \\end{vmatrix}$, we use the expansion method along the first row:\n\n$\\Delta = 1 \\begin{vmatrix} 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} - (-4) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} + (-5) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}$\n$\\Delta = 1((2)(-2) - (3)(1)) + 4((1)(-2) - (3)(-3)) - 5((1)(1) - (2)(-3))$\n$\\Delta = 1(-4 - 3) + 4(-2 + 9) - 5(1 + 6)$\n$\\Delta = 1(-7) + 4(7) - 5(7)$\n$\\Delta = -7 + 28 - 35 = -14$\n\nThe calculated determinant is -14, which corresponds to option G.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
