    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the inverse Laplace transform L^-1[1 / {{s(s^2 + 1)}}], using the convolution.\n\nOptions: \nA. sin t - t\nB. 1 - cos t\nC. t sin t\nD. e^t - 1\nE. 1 - e^-t\nF. sin t\nG. e^t - cos t\nH. t - sin t\nI. 1 + cos t\nJ. - cos t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s) = \\frac{1}{s(s^2+1)}$ using convolution, we identify it as the product of $G(s) = \\frac{1}{s}$ and $H(s) = \\frac{1}{s^2+1}$. The inverse transforms are $g(t) = 1$ and $h(t) = \\sin t$.\n\nUsing the convolution theorem:\n$\\mathcal{L}^{-1}[G(s)H(s)] = \\int_{0}^{t} g(t-\\tau)h(\\tau) \\, d\\tau = \\int_{0}^{t} 1 \\cdot \\sin \\tau \\, d\\tau$\n$= [-\\cos \\tau]_{0}^{t} = -\\cos t - (-\\cos 0) = 1 - \\cos t$.\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, it matches option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
