    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10381",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Prescribe, by an appropriate unit vector, the direction in which a positive test charge should be moved from (1, 3, - 1) in the fieldE= - xa_x + ya_y + 3a_z to experience (a) a maximum opposing force; (b) a maximum aiding force.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.688a_x + 0.229a_y + 0.688a_z, -0.688a_x - 0.229a_y - 0.688a_z\nB. 0.229a_x + 0.229a_y + 0.688a_z, -0.229a_x - 0.229a_y - 0.688a_z\nC. 0.229a_x - 0.688a_y + 0.688a_z, - 0.229a_x + 0.688a_y - 0.688a_z\nD. 0.229a_x + 0.688a_y + 0.229a_z, -0.229a_x - 0.688a_y - 0.229a_z\nE. 0.229a_x - 0.688a_y - 0.688a_z, - 0.229a_x + 0.688a_y + 0.688a_z\nF. 0.688a_x - 0.229a_y + 0.229a_z, -0.688a_x + 0.229a_y - 0.229a_z\nG. 0.688a_x + 0.688a_y - 0.229a_z, -0.688a_x - 0.688a_y + 0.229a_z\nH. -0.229a_x + 0.688a_y + 0.688a_z, 0.229a_x - 0.688a_y - 0.688a_z\nI. 0.688a_x - 0.229a_y - 0.688a_z, - 0.688a_x + 0.229a_y + 0.688a_z\nJ. 0.688a_x - 0.688a_y + 0.229a_z, - 0.688a_x + 0.688a_y - 0.229a_z\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the direction of the force on a positive test charge, we evaluate the electric field $\\mathbf{E} = -x\\mathbf{a}_x + y\\mathbf{a}_y + 3\\mathbf{a}_z$ at the point $(1, 3, -1)$:\n$\\mathbf{E} = -(1)\\mathbf{a}_x + (3)\\mathbf{a}_y + 3\\mathbf{a}_z = -\\mathbf{a}_x + 3\\mathbf{a}_y + 3\\mathbf{a}_z$.\n\nThe force experienced by a positive charge is in the direction of the electric field ($\\mathbf{F} = q\\mathbf{E}$). \n(a) For a **maximum opposing force**, the charge must be moved in the direction opposite to the electric field: $-\\mathbf{E} = \\mathbf{a}_x - 3\\mathbf{a}_y - 3\\mathbf{a}_z$. \nThe unit vector is $\\frac{\\mathbf{a}_x - 3\\mathbf{a}_y - 3\\mathbf{a}_z}{\\sqrt{1^2 + (-3)^2 + (-3)^2}} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a}_x - 3\\mathbf{a}_y - 3\\mathbf{a}_z}{\\sqrt{19}} \\approx 0.229\\mathbf{a}_x - 0.688\\mathbf{a}_y - 0.688\\mathbf{a}_z$.\n\n(b) For a **maximum aiding force**, the charge must be moved in the direction of the electric field: $\\mathbf{E} = -\\mathbf{a}_x + 3\\mathbf{a}_y + 3\\mathbf{a}_z$.\nThe unit vector is $\\frac{-\\mathbf{a}_x + 3\\mathbf{a}_y + 3\\mathbf{a}_z}{\\sqrt{19}} \\approx -0.229\\mathbf{a}_x + 0.688\\mathbf{a}_y + 0.688\\mathbf{a}_z$.\n\nComparing these results to the options, Option E matches these vectors.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
