    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the eigenvalues, we solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A - \\lambda I) = 0$ for each matrix:\n\n1.  **Matrix (a)** $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\end{pmatrix}$: $\\det \\begin{pmatrix} 3-\\lambda & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{pmatrix} = (3-\\lambda)^2 - 1 = \\lambda^2 - 6\\lambda + 8 = (\\lambda-4)(\\lambda-2)$. Eigenvalues are **4, 2**.\n2.  **Matrix (b)** $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\end{pmatrix}$: The sum of eigenvalues (trace) is $2+3+2=7$. Testing options with 4, 2: $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = (2-\\lambda)[(3-\\lambda)(2-\\lambda)-2] - 2[(2-\\lambda)-1] + 1[2-(3-\\lambda)] = 0$. Solving results in $\\lambda = 1, 1, 5$ (Check: Trace $1+1+5=7$; Determinant $1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 5 = 5$).\n3.  **Matrix (c)** $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 4 & 6 \\\\ -8 & 0 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}$: The sum of eigenvalues (trace) is $2+4-3=3$. Testing Option I: $1 + (-1) + 3 = 3$. Check determinant: $2(-12) - (-1)(-27+48) + 0 = -24 + 21 = -3$. Product of eigenvalues: $1 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot 3 = -3$.\n\nComparing these results to the options, Option I matches all three matrices.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
