    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For a random variable $X$ uniformly distributed over the interval $[a, b]$, the variance is calculated using the formula:\n$$\\text{Var}(X) = \\frac{(b - a)^2}{12}$$\nSubstituting $a = 0$ and $b = 3$:\n$$\\text{Var}(X) = \\frac{(3 - 0)^2}{12} = \\frac{9}{12} = \\frac{3}{4}$$\n\n\\boxed{C}",
