    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10546",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the partial-fraction expansion of F(s) = [(8s + 2) / (s^2 + 3s + 2)]\n\nOptions: \nA. F(s) = [(-2) / (s + 1)] + [(-8) / (s + 2)]\nB. F(s) = [(8) / (s + 1)] + [(- 10) / (s + 2)]\nC. F(s) = [(8) / (s + 2)] + [(2) / (s + 1)]\nD. F(s) = [(-8) / (s + 1)] + [(-2) / (s + 2)]\nE. F(s) = [(6) / (s + 2)] + [(-14) / (s + 1)]\nF. F(s) = [(- 6) / (s + 1)] + [(-14) / (s + 2)]\nG. F(s) = [(- 6) / (s + 2)] + [14 / (s + 1)]\nH. F(s) = [(- 6) / (s + 1)] + [14 / (s + 2)]\nI. F(s) = [(6) / (s + 1)] + [14 / (s + 2)]\nJ. F(s) = [(2) / (s + 1)] + [(6) / (s + 2)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the partial-fraction expansion of $F(s) = \\frac{8s + 2}{s^2 + 3s + 2}$, we first factor the denominator:\n$s^2 + 3s + 2 = (s + 1)(s + 2)$.\n\nWe set up the partial fraction form:\n$F(s) = \\frac{A}{s+1} + \\frac{B}{s+2}$\n\nUsing the cover-up method:\nFor $A$ (at $s = -1$): $A = \\frac{8(-1) + 2}{-1 + 2} = \\frac{-6}{1} = -6$.\nFor $B$ (at $s = -2$): $B = \\frac{8(-2) + 2}{-2 + 1} = \\frac{-14}{-1} = 14$.\n\nThus, $F(s) = \\frac{-6}{s+1} + \\frac{14}{s+2}$, which corresponds to option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
