  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10267",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine those values of s for which the improper integral G(s) = ^\\infty\\int0e^-st dt converges, and find the Laplace transform of f(t) = 1.\n\nOptions: \nA. G(s) diverges for all values of s\nB. G(s) converges for all values of s\nC. G(s) converges to (1 / s) for Re{{s) > 0 and diverges otherwise. The required Laplace transform is L{{1}} = (1 / s), for Re{{s) > 0\nD. G(s) converges for Re{{s}} = 0 and the required Laplace transform is L{{1}} = (2 / s^2)\nE. G(s) converges to (1 / s) for Re{{s) < 0 and diverges otherwise\nF. G(s) converges to (2 / s) for Re{{s}} > 2 and diverges otherwise\nG. The required Laplace transform is L{{1}} = (1 / s^2), for Re{{s}} > 1\nH. G(s) converges to (s / 2) for Re{{s}} > 1 and diverges otherwise\nI. G(s) converges for s = 0 only\nJ. The required Laplace transform is L{{1}} = (s), for Re{{s) > 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the convergence of the integral $G(s) = \\int_{0}^{\\infty} e^{-st} dt$, we evaluate the definite integral:\n$\\int_{0}^{T} e^{-st} dt = \\left[ \\frac{e^{-st}}{-s} \\right]_{0}^{T} = \\frac{1 - e^{-sT}}{s}$.\n\nFor the integral to converge as $T \\to \\infty$, the term $e^{-sT}$ must approach 0, which occurs if and only if the real part of $s$ is positive ($\\text{Re}\\{s\\} > 0$). In this case, the integral converges to $1/s$. This result represents the Laplace transform of the constant function $f(t) = 1$.\n\nComparing this result to the options, Option C correctly identifies the convergence criteria ($\\text{Re}\\{s\\} > 0$), the value of the integral ($1/s$), and the resulting Laplace transform.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
