    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10014",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Findcurlaat the point (1, - 2, 1) fora= x^2y^2i+ 2xyzj+ z^2k(1)\n\nOptions: \nA. (4, 4, 0)\nB. (-2, 0, 0)\nC. (0, 0, 4)\nD. (4, 0, 0)\nE. (2, 0, 0)\nF. (6, 0, 0)\nG. (0, -4, 0)\nH. (0, 2, 0)\nI. (2, 4, 2)\nJ. (0, 4, 0)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the curl of the vector field $\\mathbf{a} = x^2y^2\\mathbf{i} + 2xyz\\mathbf{j} + z^2\\mathbf{k}$, we use the determinant formula for curl:\n$$\\text{curl } \\mathbf{a} = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} \\\\ x^2y^2 & 2xyz & z^2 \\end{vmatrix}$$\nCalculating the components:\n- $i$-component: $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(z^2) - \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}(2xyz) = 0 - 2xy = -2xy$\n- $j$-component: $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}(x^2y^2) - \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(z^2) = 0 - 0 = 0$\n- $k$-component: $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(2xyz) - \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(x^2y^2) = 2yz - 2x^2y$\n\nNow, evaluate the curl at the point $(1, -2, 1)$:\n- $i$-component: $-2(1)(-2) = 4$\n- $j$-component: $0$\n- $k$-component: $2(-2)(1) - 2(1)^2(-2) = -4 + 4 = 0$\n\nThe resulting vector is $(4, 0, 0)$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
