    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10566",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the inverse Laplace transform L^-1 {{1 / (s - 1)^2}}, using the convolution.\n\nOptions: \nA. t^2e^t\nB. t e^2t\nC. e^(-t)\nD. t^3e^t\nE. te^t\nF. t^2e^(-t)\nG. e^t\nH. e^t * cos(t)\nI. e^2t\nJ. e^t * sin(t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s) = \\frac{1}{(s-1)^2}$ using the convolution theorem, we recognize that $F(s)$ can be written as the product of two functions: $G(s) = \\frac{1}{s-1}$ and $H(s) = \\frac{1}{s-1}$.\n\nThe inverse Laplace transform of $\\frac{1}{s-1}$ is $g(t) = e^t$. According to the convolution theorem, $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\{G(s)H(s)\\} = (g * h)(t)$:\n$$(e^t * e^t) = \\int_0^t e^\\tau e^{t-\\tau} d\\tau = \\int_0^t e^t d\\tau = e^t [\\tau]_0^t = t e^t$$\n\nComparing this result to the given options, it matches option E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
