    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10176",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the Laplace transform L{{g(t)}}, where g(t)= 0,t < 4 and= (t - 4)^2,t \\geq 4\n\nOptions: \nA. [(2e^-4s) / s^3]\nB. 2 / s^3\nC. (2 / s^2) * e^-4s\nD. 4 / s^3\nE. [(2e^-4s) / s^4]\nF. (2 / s^3) * e^-s\nG. e^-4s\nH. [(e^-4s) / s^2]\nI. (2 / s) * e^-4s\nJ. (t^2 - 8t + 16) / s\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the Laplace transform of the function $g(t)$, we recognize that it is a shifted function defined as:\n$g(t) = (t - 4)^2 u(t - 4)$, where $u(t-4)$ is the unit step function.\n\nUsing the second shifting theorem, $\\mathcal{L}\\{f(t-a)u(t-a)\\} = e^{-as} F(s)$, where $F(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\{f(t)\\}$.\nIn this case, $f(t) = t^2$ and $a = 4$.\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t) = t^2$ is $F(s) = \\frac{2!}{s^{2+1}} = \\frac{2}{s^3}$.\n\nApplying the theorem:\n$\\mathcal{L}\\{g(t)\\} = e^{-4s} \\cdot \\frac{2}{s^3} = \\frac{2e^{-4s}}{s^3}$.\n\nComparing this result to the options, it matches Option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
