    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10335",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given that the joint density function of X and Y is f(x, y) = 6x^2ywhere 0 < x < 1 and 0 < y < 1, = 0elsewhere, find Pr[0 < x < (3/4), (1/3) < y < 2].\n\nOptions: \nA. 3/4\nB. 2/3\nC. 1/4\nD. 5/8\nE. 7/8\nF. 1/8\nG. 1/2\nH. 3/8\nI. 11/24\nJ. 9/16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability $\\text{Pr}[0 < X < 3/4, 1/3 < Y < 2]$, we integrate the joint density function $f(x, y) = 6x^2y$ over the region defined by the constraints and the support of the function ($0 < x < 1$ and $0 < y < 1$).\n\nThe effective integration limits are $x \\in [0, 3/4]$ and $y \\in [1/3, 1]$:\n$$\\text{Pr} = \\int_{1/3}^{1} \\int_{0}^{3/4} 6x^2y \\, dx \\, dy$$\n\nFirst, integrate with respect to $x$:\n$$\\int_{0}^{3/4} 6x^2y \\, dx = [2x^3y]_{0}^{3/4} = 2\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^3y = 2\\left(\\frac{27}{64}\\right)y = \\frac{27}{32}y$$\n\nNext, integrate with respect to $y$:\n$$\\int_{1/3}^{1} \\frac{27}{32}y \\, dy = \\left[\\frac{27}{64}y^2\\right]_{1/3}^{1} = \\frac{27}{64}\\left(1^2 - \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2\\right) = \\frac{27}{64}\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{9}\\right) = \\frac{27}{64} \\cdot \\frac{8}{9}$$\n\nSimplifying the expression:\n$$\\frac{27}{9} \\cdot \\frac{8}{64} = 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{3}{8}$$\n\nThe correct letter choice is H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
