    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the Laplace transforms, we start with the basic transform $\\mathcal{L}\\{e^{kt}\\} = \\frac{1}{s-k}$. Using the definitions of the hyperbolic and trigonometric functions:\n\n1.  $\\cosh kt = \\frac{e^{kt} + e^{-kt}}{2} \\implies \\mathcal{L}\\{\\cosh kt\\} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{1}{s-k} + \\frac{1}{s+k} \\right) = \\frac{s}{s^2 - k^2}$\n2.  $\\sinh kt = \\frac{e^{kt} - e^{-kt}}{2} \\implies \\mathcal{L}\\{\\sinh kt\\} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{1}{s-k} - \\frac{1}{s+k} \\right) = \\frac{k}{s^2 - k^2}$\n3.  $\\cos kt = \\cosh(ikt) \\implies \\mathcal{L}\\{\\cos kt\\} = \\frac{s}{s^2 - (ik)^2} = \\frac{s}{s^2 + k^2}$\n4.  $\\sin kt = \\frac{\\sinh(ikt)}{i} \\implies \\mathcal{L}\\{\\sin kt\\} = \\frac{1}{i} \\frac{ik}{s^2 - (ik)^2} = \\frac{k}{s^2 + k^2}$\n\nComparing these results to the given options, Option J matches exactly.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
