  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10377",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the steady-state solution of the equation y [n] + [1 / \\surd(3)]y [n - 1] =cos(\\pi/6) n.\n\nOptions: \nA. y_ss[n] = \\surd(3/7)cos[(\\pi/6)n tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{2\\surd(3)}}]\nB. y_ss[n] = \\surd(2/7)sin[(\\pi/6)n + tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\nC. y_ss[n] = \\surd(2/7)cos[(\\pi/6)n tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\nD. y_ss[n] = \\surd(3/7)cos[(\\pi/3)n tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\nE. y_ss[n] = \\surd(3/7)sin[(\\pi/6)n tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\nF. y_ss[n] = \\surd(3/8)sin[(\\pi/6)n - tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\nG. y_ss[n] = \\surd(3/7)cos[(\\pi/6)n tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\nH. y_ss[n] = \\surd(3/7)sin[(\\pi/6)n - tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{2\\surd(3)}}]\nI. y_ss[n] = \\surd(3/7)cos[(\\pi/6)n + tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\nJ. y_ss[n] = \\surd(1/7)cos[(\\pi/6)n tan^-1 [{{1}} / {{3\\surd(3)}}]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the steady-state solution of the difference equation $y[n] + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}y[n-1] = \\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{6}n)$, we use the phasor method. \n\n1. **Identify the input and system**: The input is $x[n] = \\cos(\\omega n)$ with $\\omega = \\pi/6$. The transfer function is $H(z) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}z^{-1}}$.\n2. **Evaluate $H(e^{j\\omega})$**:\n   $H(e^{j\\pi/6}) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(\\cos(\\pi/6) - j\\sin(\\pi/6))} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - j\\frac{1}{2})} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{2} - j\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{3}{2} - j\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}}$.\n3. **Calculate Magnitude and Phase**:\n   Magnitude $|H(e^{j\\pi/6})| = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(\\frac{3}{2})^2 + (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}})^2}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4} + \\frac{1}{12}}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{27+1}{12}}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{28}{12}}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{7}}$.\n   Phase $\\angle H(e^{j\\pi/6}) = -\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{-1/2\\sqrt{3}}{3/2}\\right) = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$. (Note: The phase of the denominator is $-\\tan^{-1}(\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}})$, so the phase of $H$ is positive).\n4. **Steady-state solution**: $y_{ss}[n] = \\sqrt{3/7} \\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{6}n + \\tan^{-1}(\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}}))$.\n\nComparing this result to the options, Option I matches perfectly.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 538,
