    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10939",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given the Laplace transform of i(t), L[i(t)] = I(s) = [{{E - V(0^+)}} / {{R(s + (1 / RC))}}] Determine i(0^+).\n\nOptions: \nA. [{{E / (v(0^+) * R)}}]\nB. [{{v(0^+) - E}} / R]\nC. [{{E * v(0^+)}} / R]\nD. [{{E - v(0^+)}} * R]\nE. [{{E * R}} / {{v(0^+) - 1}}]\nF. [{{E + R}} / {{v(0^+) + RC}}]\nG. [{{(E - v(0^+)) / (R + RC)}}]\nH. [{{E + v(0^+)}} / R]\nI. [{{E * (v(0^+) + 1)}} / R]\nJ. [{{E - v(0^+)}} / R]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the initial value $i(0^+)$, we use the **Initial Value Theorem** for Laplace transforms, which states that:\n$i(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} s I(s)$\n\nGiven the expression:\n$I(s) = \\frac{E - v(0^+)}{R(s + \\frac{1}{RC})}$\n\nApplying the theorem:\n$i(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} s \\left[ \\frac{E - v(0^+)}{R(s + \\frac{1}{RC})} \\right] = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} \\frac{s}{s + \\frac{1}{RC}} \\cdot \\frac{E - v(0^+)}{R}$\n\nSince $\\lim_{s \\to \\infty} \\frac{s}{s + \\frac{1}{RC}} = 1$, the result is:\n$i(0^+) = \\frac{E - v(0^+)}{R}$\n\nComparing this result to the options, it matches Option J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 300,
        "output_tokens": 243,
