    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10346",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the Fourier transform of the function f(t) = e^-2t sin(6t - 18) u(t - 3) where u(t) is the unit step function. Note: F[e^-\\alphat(sin \\omega_0t)u(t)] = [\\omega_0 / {{(\\alpha + j\\omega)^2 + \\omega_0^2}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. 6e^-6 [e^-3jω / {{(jω - 2)^2 + 36}}]\nB. 6e^-2 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 36}}]\nC. 3e^-6 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 36}}]\nD. 6e^-18 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 36}}]\nE. 6e^-6 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 72}}]\nF. 6e^-6 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 36}}]\nG. 3e^-2 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 18}}]\nH. 6e^-6 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 18}}]\nI. 6 [e^-3jω / {{(jω + 2)^2 + 36}}]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the Fourier transform of $f(t) = e^{-2t} \\sin(6t - 18) u(t - 3)$, we first perform a change of variable to align the function with the unit step $u(t-3)$. Let $\\tau = t - 3$, then $t = \\tau + 3$.\n\nSubstituting these into the function:\n$f(\\tau + 3) = e^{-2(\\tau + 3)} \\sin(6(\\tau + 3) - 18) u(\\tau) = e^{-6} e^{-2\\tau} \\sin(6\\tau) u(\\tau)$.\n\nUsing the provided Fourier transform formula $F[e^{-\\alpha t} \\sin(\\omega_0 t) u(t)] = \\frac{\\omega_0}{(\\alpha + j\\omega)^2 + \\omega_0^2}$ with $\\alpha = 2$ and $\\omega_0 = 6$, the transform of $e^{-2\\tau} \\sin(6\\tau) u(\\tau)$ is $\\frac{6}{(2 + j\\omega)^2 + 36}$.\n\nBy the time-shifting property of the Fourier transform, $f(t - t_0) \\leftrightarrow e^{-j\\omega t_0} F(\\omega)$. Here $t_0 = 3$, and the constant multiplier is $e^{-6}$. Therefore:\n$F(\\omega) = e^{-6} \\cdot e^{-3j\\omega} \\cdot \\frac{6}{(j\\omega + 2)^2 + 36} = \\frac{6e^{-6} e^{-3j\\omega}}{(j\\omega + 2)^2 + 36}$.\n\nThis matches Option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
