    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10016",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What inductance is required to resonate at 10 MHz with a capacitance of 100 pF?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.00 μH\nB. 1.53 μH\nC. 3.14 μH\nD. 3.53 μH\nE. 0.75 μH\nF. 2.00 μH\nG. 5.00 μH\nH. 4.00 μH\nI. 1.77 μH\nJ. 2.53 μH\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the required inductance for resonance, we use the resonance formula:\n$f = \\frac{1}{2\\pi\\sqrt{LC}}$\n\nRearranging the formula to solve for $L$:\n$L = \\frac{1}{(2\\pi f)^2 C}$\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n$f = 10 \\times 10^6 \\text{ Hz}$\n$C = 100 \\times 10^{-12} \\text{ F}$\n$L = \\frac{1}{(2\\pi \\times 10^7)^2 \\times 100 \\times 10^{-12}} = \\frac{1}{(4\\pi^2 \\times 10^{14}) \\times 10^{-10}} = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 \\times 10^4} \\approx \\frac{1}{39.478 \\times 10,000} \\approx 2.533 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{ H}$\n\n$L \\approx 2.53 \\mu\\text{H}$\n\n\\boxed{J}",
