    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10330",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The transfer function of an RC low-pass filter is given as H(f) = [1 / {{1 +jf/f_c}}] wheref_cis the 3-dB frequency. If the input to this filter is a white noise, find the output noise power N_0 of the filter.\n\nOptions: \nA. \\((\\eta f_c\\pi) / 8\\)\nB. \\(5(\\eta f_c\\pi) / 2\\)\nC. (\\etaf_c\\pi) / 3\nD. \\(\\eta f_c\\)\nE. (\\etaf_c\\pi) / 2\nF. (\\etaf_c\\pi) / 4\nG. \\(3(\\eta f_c\\pi) / 4\\)\nH. \\(4(\\eta f_c\\pi)\\)\nI. 2(\\etaf_c\\pi)\nJ. \\(\\eta f_c / \\pi\\)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the output noise power $N_0$ of an RC low-pass filter when the input is white noise with a power spectral density $\\eta$ (usually denoted as $S_{in}(f) = \\eta/2$ for one-sided or $\\eta$ for double-sided, but in the context of these options, $\\eta$ typically represents the single-sided PSD), we integrate the input PSD multiplied by the squared magnitude of the transfer function $|H(f)|^2$ over all positive frequencies.\n\nThe calculation is as follows:\n\\[ N_0 = \\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\eta |H(f)|^2 df = \\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\eta \\frac{1}{1 + (f/f_c)^2} df \\]\nUsing the standard integral $\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2} dx = \\tan^{-1}(x)$, we get:\n\\[ N_0 = \\eta \\cdot f_c \\left[ \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{f}{f_c}\\right) \\right]_{0}^{\\infty} = \\eta f_c \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 0 \\right) = \\frac{\\eta f_c \\pi}{2} \\]\n\nThis matches Option E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 281,
        "output_tokens": 283,
