    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10292",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A long cylindrical log of specific gravity (2/3) will float in water with its axis horizontal. As its length gradually is reduced it will float in the same position. If its length is reduced so that it is only a fraction of its diameter, it will float with its axis vertical. What is its diairieter-to-length ratio for which it will just float with its axis vertical?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.5\nB. 2.5\nC. 1.33\nD. 0.8\nE. 2.0\nF. 0.5\nG. 1.1\nH. 1.75\nI. 1.0\nJ. 1.25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the stability of a floating cylinder, we analyze the transition between horizontal and vertical floating positions. For a cylinder to float stably in a vertical position, the metacentric height ($MG$) must be greater than or equal to zero.\n\nThe formula for the stability of a vertical floating cylinder is:\n$MG = \\frac{I}{V_{sub}} - BG \\geq 0$, where $I$ is the area moment of inertia of the waterplane ($\\frac{\\pi D^4}{64}$), $V_{sub}$ is the submerged volume ($\\frac{\\pi D^2}{4} h$), and $BG$ is the distance between the center of buoyancy and center of gravity.\nGiven the specific gravity $s = 2/3$, the submerged depth is $h = sL$ and the distance $BG = \\frac{L}{2} - \\frac{sL}{2} = \\frac{L(1-s)}{2}$.\nSubstituting these into the stability condition:\n$\\frac{\\pi D^4 / 64}{\\pi D^2 s L / 4} \\geq \\frac{L(1-s)}{2} \\implies \\frac{D^2}{16sL} \\geq \\frac{L(1-s)}{2} \\implies \\frac{D^2}{L^2} \\geq 8s(1-s)$.\nPlugging in $s = 2/3$:\n$\\frac{D^2}{L^2} \\geq 8(\\frac{2}{3})(1 - \\frac{2}{3}) = 8(\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{1}{3}) = \\frac{16}{9}$.\nTaking the square root: $\\frac{D}{L} \\geq \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{9}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.33$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 229,
        "output_tokens": 413,
        "total_tokens": 642
      },
