    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10303",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate \\nablaf at the point (2, 3,5). The scalar field f is given by f(x_1, x_2, x_3) = 2 sin x_1 - x_1^2x_2x_3 + x_1e^(x)2(1)\n\nOptions: \nA. (40.74, -20.17, 12)\nB. (- 30.74, 10.17, - 2)\nC. (0, 40.34, 24)\nD. (30.74, 10.17, 2)\nE. (40.74, 20.17, -12)\nF. (- 40.74, 20.17, - 12)\nG. (30.74, -20.17, -12)\nH. (-40.74, -20.17, 12)\nI. (-30.74, -10.17, 2)\nJ. (40.74, 20.17, 12)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the gradient $\\nabla f$ at the point $(2, 3, 5)$, we calculate the partial derivatives of $f(x_1, x_2, x_3) = 2\\sin x_1 - x_1^2x_2x_3 + x_1e^{x_2}$ (assuming the typo $e^{(x)2(1)}$ refers to $e^{x_2}$).\n\n1.  **Partial with respect to $x_1$**: $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x_1} = 2\\cos x_1 - 2x_1x_2x_3 + e^{x_2}$.\n    At $(2, 3, 5)$: $2\\cos(2) - 2(2)(3)(5) + e^3 \\approx 2(-0.416) - 60 + 20.085 \\approx -0.832 - 60 + 20.085 \\approx -40.747$.\n2.  **Partial with respect to $x_2$**: $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x_2} = -x_1^2x_3 + x_1e^{x_2}$.\n    At $(2, 3, 5)$: $-(2^2)(5) + 2e^3 \\approx -20 + 2(20.085) \\approx -20 + 40.17 \\approx 20.17$.\n3.  **Partial with respect to $x_3$**: $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x_3} = -x_1^2x_2$.\n    At $(2, 3, 5)$: $-(2^2)(3) = -12$.\n\nCombining these, $\\nabla f(2, 3, 5) \\approx (-40.74, 20.17, -12)$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
