    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10720",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the Laplace transform of f(t) = t^2.\n\nOptions: \nA. (2 / s^4)\nB. (1 / s^3)\nC. (t^2 / s)\nD. (t^2 / s^3)\nE. (2 / s^3)\nF. (4 / s^3)\nG. (3 / s^4)\nH. (2 / s^2)\nI. (3 / s^3)\nJ. (1 / s^2)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The general formula for the Laplace transform of $f(t) = t^n$ is $\\mathcal{L}\\{t^n\\} = \\frac{n!}{s^{n+1}}$ for $n > -1$. For $f(t) = t^2$, we have $n = 2$, so the transform is $\\frac{2!}{s^{2+1}} = \\frac{2 \\times 1}{s^3} = \\frac{2}{s^3}$. Comparing this result to the given options, it matches Option E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
