    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Five capacitors each of 5 µF are connected in series, the equivalent capacitance of the system will be\n\nOptions: \nA. 15 µF\nB. 10 µF\nC. 5 µF\nD. 0.1 µF\nE. 2 µF\nF. 0.5 µF\nG. 30 µF\nH. 1 µF\nI. 25 µF\nJ. 20 µF\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For capacitors connected in series, the equivalent capacitance $C_{eq}$ is calculated using the formula:\n$\\frac{1}{C_{eq}} = \\frac{1}{C_1} + \\frac{1}{C_2} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{C_n}$\n\nSince all five capacitors have the same value ($C = 5\\text{ µF}$), the formula simplifies to:\n$C_{eq} = \\frac{C}{n} = \\frac{5\\text{ µF}}{5} = 1\\text{ µF}$\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, the correct answer is 1 µF.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
