    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_9981",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What will be the number of lamps, each having 300 lumens, required to obtain an average illuminance of 50 lux on a 4m * 3m rectangular room?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6\nB. 1\nC. 2\nD. 5\nE. 7\nF. 3\nG. 9\nH. 10\nI. 8\nJ. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of lamps required, we use the basic formula for illuminance:\n$\\text{Illuminance (Lux)} = \\frac{\\text{Total Lumens}}{\\text{Area}}$\n\n1.  **Calculate the area of the room:** $4\\text{m} \\times 3\\text{m} = 12\\text{m}^2$.\n2.  **Calculate the total lumens required:** $\\text{Total Lumens} = \\text{Illuminance} \\times \\text{Area} = 50\\text{ lux} \\times 12\\text{m}^2 = 600\\text{ lumens}$.\n3.  **Calculate the number of lamps:** $\\text{Number of lamps} = \\frac{\\text{Total Lumens}}{\\text{Lumens per lamp}} = \\frac{600}{300} = 2$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
