  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10309",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the solution for the equationX=AX+bu;X(0) = X_0 where A=\\vert10\\vert,b=\\vert1\\vert,X_0 =\\vert- 1\\vert, \\vert- 22\\vert\\vert2\\vert\\vert0\\vert u(t) = \\delta(t) (impulse function).\n\nOptions: \nA. -3\nB. 2\nC. 0\nD. 3\nE. 10\nF. -2\nG. 22\nH. 1\nI. -10\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the solution for the state-space equation $\\dot{X} = AX + bu$ with $u(t) = \\delta(t)$, we use the formula for the state response:\n$X(t) = e^{At}X_0 + \\int_{0}^{t} e^{A(t-\\tau)}b\\delta(\\tau)d\\tau = e^{At}(X_0 + b)$.\n\nGiven the values:\n$A = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$ (interpreting $\\vert 1 \\quad 0 \\vert$ as a matrix structure), $b = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}$, and $X_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -22 \\end{pmatrix}$.\nWait, looking at the provided values $\\vert 1 \\quad 0 \\vert$ and $\\vert 1 \\vert \\vert 2 \\vert \\vert 0 \\vert$ is ambiguous, but typically in these specific textbook problems, we evaluate $X(0^+)$ immediately after the impulse.\n$X(0^+) = X_0 + b = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -22 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 22 \\end{pmatrix}$ (assuming the vertical bar implies vectors/matrices).\nHowever, if we look at the provided options, they are scalars. If the question asks for a specific component or the sum, and based on the provided $X_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -22 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 22 \\end{pmatrix}$, then $X(0^+) = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$. If $b$ is meant to be $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $X_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$, the result is $0$. Given the options and the likely structure of the problem, the resulting state immediately after the impulse $\\delta(t)$ is $0$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 208,
        "output_tokens": 480,
        "total_tokens": 688
