    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10316",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Design a bar to resist pure tension of 4000 lb., based on a factor of safety of 2.5. Tensile strength of the material = 175 psi.\n\nOptions: \nA. 14 in. × 3 in.\nB. 16 in. × 4 in.\nC. 18 in. × 6 in.\nD. 15 in. × 5 in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the required area of the bar, we first determine the allowable stress:\n$\\text{Allowable Stress} = \\frac{\\text{Tensile Strength}}{\\text{Factor of Safety}} = \\frac{175 \\text{ psi}}{2.5} = 70 \\text{ psi}$.\n\nThe required cross-sectional area is:\n$\\text{Area} = \\frac{\\text{Force}}{\\text{Allowable Stress}} = \\frac{4000 \\text{ lb}}{70 \\text{ psi}} \\approx 57.14 \\text{ in}^2$.\n\nChecking the options for the area:\nA. $14 \\times 3 = 42 \\text{ in}^2$\nB. $16 \\times 4 = 64 \\text{ in}^2$\nC. $18 \\times 6 = 108 \\text{ in}^2$\nD. $15 \\times 5 = 75 \\text{ in}^2$\n\nOption B is the smallest area that exceeds the required $57.14 \\text{ in}^2$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
