    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10039",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Apreemphasiscircuit of transfer function \\vertHp(f)\\vert^2 = k^2f^2 is used in an FM system, with the modulating signal having spectral density of G(f) = [{{G_o}} / {{1 + (f / f_1)^2}}] where f_1 << f_m. Determine a suitable value of k^2 such thatpreemphasisdoes not affect the bandwidth of the channel.\n\nOptions: \nA. k^2 \\geq [{{\\pi}} / {{f_1(2f_m - \\pif_1)}}]\nB. k^2 \\leq [{{\\pi}} / {{2f_1(2f_m + \\pif_1)}}]\nC. k^2 \\leq [{{2\\pi}} / {{(f_1 + f_m)(2f_m)}}]\nD. k^2 \\leq [{{\\pi}} / {{f_1(2f_m)}}]\nE. k^2 \\leq [{{4\\pi}} / {{f_1(2f_m)}}]\nF. k^2 \\leq [{{\\pi}} / {{(f_1 + f_m)(2f_m - \\pif_1)}}]\nG. k^2 \\leq [{{\\pi}} / {{f_1(f_m - \\pif_1)}}]\nH. k^2 \\leq [{{2\\pi}} / {{f_1(2f_m - \\pif_1)}}]\nI. k^2 \\leq [{{\\pi}} / {{f_1(2f_m - \\pif_1)}}]\nJ. k^2 \\leq [{{\\pi}} / {{f_1(2f_m + \\pif_1)}}]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the suitable value of $k^2$, we analyze the power spectral density (PSD) of the signal after pre-emphasis. The PSD of the pre-emphasized signal is given by $S_{pe}(f) = |H_p(f)|^2 G(f) = k^2 f^2 \\frac{G_0}{1 + (f/f_1)^2}$.\n\nFor pre-emphasis to not affect the bandwidth of the channel (meaning the noise power is not increased excessively or the signal power remains within the limits of the channel bandwidth $f_m$), the condition typically involves ensuring the total power of the pre-emphasized signal does not exceed a specific threshold relative to the original signal or the channel noise. Integrating the PSD from $0$ to $f_m$ and comparing it to the constraints of the system leads to the derived inequality $k^2 \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{f_1(2f_m - \\pi f_1)}$ under specific engineering approximations for FM pre-emphasis circuits.\n\nComparing this result to the given options, Option I matches the derived mathematical form.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
