    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10194",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A carrier with amplitude 4 volts and frequencyf_c= 2MHz is frequency modulated by a modulating signal m(t) = sin 1000\\pit. The amplitude of the modulating signal is 2 volts and the frequency deviation was found to be equal to 1 kHz. If the amplitude and frequency of the modulating signal are increased to 8 volts and 2 kHz respectively, write an expression for the new modulated signal.\n\nOptions: \nA. v(t) = 4cos(4\\pi × 10^6 t + 2 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nB. v(t) = 8cos(4π × 10^6 t + 4 sin2π × 1000t)\nC. v(t) = 8cos(2π × 10^6 t + 4 sin2π × 2000t)\nD. v(t) = 8cos(4π × 10^6 t + 8 sin2π × 2000t)\nE. v(t) = 4cos(4π × 10^6 t + 16 sin2π × 2000t)\nF. v(t) = 4cos(4π × 10^6 t + 4 sin2π × 1000t)\nG. v(t) = 4cos(2\\pi × 10^6 t + 2 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nH. v(t) = 4cos(4\\pi × 10^6 t + 4 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nI. v(t) = 8cos(4\\pi × 10^6 t + 2 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nJ. v(t) = 4cos(4π × 10^6 t + 8 sin2π × 2000t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the expression for the new modulated signal, we use the general formula for a frequency modulated (FM) wave: $v(t) = A_c \\cos(2\\pi f_c t + \\beta \\sin(2\\pi f_m t))$, where $\\beta = \\frac{\\Delta f}{f_m}$.\n\n1.  **Identify constants:** The carrier amplitude $A_c = 4\\text{V}$ and carrier frequency $f_c = 2\\text{MHz}$ remain constant. Thus, the term is $4 \\cos(2\\pi \\times 2 \\times 10^6 t + \\dots) = 4 \\cos(4\\pi \\times 10^6 t + \\dots)$.\n2.  **Calculate new frequency deviation ($\\Delta f_{new}$):** Frequency deviation is proportional to the amplitude of the modulating signal ($V_m$). The initial $V_{m1} = 2\\text{V}$ gave $\\Delta f_1 = 1\\text{kHz}$. The new $V_{m2} = 8\\text{V}$ (a 4-fold increase), so $\\Delta f_{new} = 1\\text{kHz} \\times (8/2) = 4\\text{kHz}$.\n3.  **Calculate new modulation index ($\\beta_{new}$):** The new modulating frequency is $f_{m2} = 2\\text{kHz}$. Thus, $\\beta_{new} = \\frac{\\Delta f_{new}}{f_{m2}} = \\frac{4\\text{kHz}}{2\\text{kHz}} = 2$.\n4.  **Formulate the equation:** $v(t) = 4 \\cos(4\\pi \\times 10^6 t + 2 \\sin(2\\pi \\times 2000 t))$.\n\nMatching this to the options, it corresponds to Option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
