  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10718",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A cast-iron flanged coupling is used to join two steel shafts 2(1/2) in., in diameter, delivering a maximum torque of 60 ft.-lb. The two halves of the couplings are joined together getherby 4 bolts, placed equidistant on a bolt circle of 3 in. diameter. If the design stress is 10,000 psi in shear for the bolt material, evaluate the diameter of the bolts.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.1280 in.\nB. 0.1260 in.\nC. 0.1220 in.\nD. 0.1255 in.\nE. 0.1215 in.\nF. 0.1236 in.\nG. 0.1250 in.\nH. 0.1240 in.\nI. 0.1200 in.\nJ. 0.1230 in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the diameter of the bolts, we start by calculating the total shear force acting on the bolt circle.\n\n1.  **Calculate Total Torque in lb-in**:\n    $T = 60 \\text{ ft-lb} \\times 12 \\text{ in/ft} = 720 \\text{ lb-in}$.\n2.  **Calculate Force per Bolt**:\n    The torque is resisted by 4 bolts at a radius ($r$) of $1.5 \\text{ in}$ (half of the $3 \\text{ in}$ diameter).\n    $F_{\\text{total}} = \\frac{T}{r} = \\frac{720}{1.5} = 480 \\text{ lb}$.\n    Force per bolt ($P$) = $\\frac{480}{4} = 120 \\text{ lb}$.\n3.  **Calculate Bolt Diameter ($d$)**:\n    Using the design stress ($\\tau = 10,000 \\text{ psi}$):\n    $\\tau = \\frac{P}{A} \\Rightarrow 10,000 = \\frac{120}{\\frac{\\pi}{4} d^2}$\n    $d^2 = \\frac{120 \\times 4}{10,000 \\times \\pi} \\approx \\frac{480}{31,415.9} \\approx 0.015278$\n    $d = \\sqrt{0.015278} \\approx 0.1236 \\text{ in}$.\n\nComparing this result to the options, it matches Option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
