    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10535",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given an electric field E=jAcos\\omega (t - (z/c)) Determine the time-dependent magnetic intensityHin free space.\n\nOptions: \nA. H= - {{jA/ c\\mu_0}}sin\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nB. H= {{iA/ c\\mu_0}}cos\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nC. H= {{kA/ c\\mu_0}}cos\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nD. H= {{kA/ c\\mu_0}}sin\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nE. H= - {{iA/ c\\mu_0}}coscos\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nF. H= {{jA/ c\\mu_0}}cos\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nG. H= - {{iA/ c\\mu_0}}sin\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nH. H= {{iA/ c\\mu_0}}coscos\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nI. H= {{iA/ c\\mu_0}}sin\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\nJ. H= {{iA\\mu_0/c}}sin\\omega {{t - (z/c)}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the magnetic intensity $\\mathbf{H}$ from the given electric field $\\mathbf{E} = \\hat{j} A \\cos[\\omega(t - z/c)]$, we use Maxwell's equations (specifically Faraday's Law: $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{E} = -\\mu_0 \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{H}}{\\partial t}$).\n\n1.  **Calculate the curl of $\\mathbf{E}$**: Since $\\mathbf{E}$ only has a $y$-component ($E_y$) and depends only on $z$, the curl is:\n    $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{E} = \\hat{i} \\frac{\\partial E_y}{\\partial z} - \\hat{k} \\frac{\\partial E_y}{\\partial x} = \\hat{i} \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} [A \\cos(\\omega(t - z/c))] = \\hat{i} [A \\sin(\\omega(t - z/c)) \\cdot \\frac{\\omega}{c}]$.\n2.  **Integrate to find $\\mathbf{H}$**: From $-\\mu_0 \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{H}}{\\partial t} = \\hat{i} \\frac{A\\omega}{c} \\sin(\\omega(t - z/c))$, we integrate with respect to $t$:\n    $\\mathbf{H} = -\\frac{1}{\\mu_0} \\int \\hat{i} \\frac{A\\omega}{c} \\sin(\\omega(t - z/c)) dt = -\\frac{1}{\\mu_0} \\hat{i} \\frac{A\\omega}{c} \\left[ -\\frac{1}{\\omega} \\cos(\\omega(t - z/c)) \\right] = \\hat{i} \\frac{A}{c\\mu_0} \\cos(\\omega(t - z/c))$.\n\nMatching this result to the options, Option B is the correct expression.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
