    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10703",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the impedance of a circuit if 100\\angle0° V causes a current7.07 + j7.07 A?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6.5 - j2.3 Ω\nB. 10 - j35 Ω\nC. 8.2 - j5.7 Ω\nD. 12.1 + j3.5 Ω\nE. 7.07 + j7.07 Ω\nF. 14 + j14 Ω\nG. 0 - j14 Ω\nH. 7.07 - j7.07 Ω\nI. 5 - j10 Ω\nJ. 10 - j7 Ω\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the impedance ($Z$), we use Ohm's law for AC circuits: $Z = \\frac{V}{I}$.\n\n1.  **Convert current to polar form:**\n    $I = 7.07 + j7.07 \\text{ A}$\n    Magnitude $|I| = \\sqrt{7.07^2 + 7.07^2} \\approx 10 \\text{ A}$\n    Angle $\\theta = \\tan^{-1}(\\frac{7.07}{7.07}) = 45^\\circ$\n    So, $I = 10\\angle45^\\circ \\text{ A}$.\n\n2.  **Calculate Impedance:**\n    $Z = \\frac{100\\angle0^\\circ \\text{ V}}{10\\angle45^\\circ \\text{ A}} = 10\\angle-45^\\circ \\Omega$\n\n3.  **Convert back to rectangular form:**\n    $Z = 10(\\cos(-45^\\circ) + j\\sin(-45^\\circ)) = 10(0.707 - j0.707) = 7.07 - j7.07 \\Omega$\n\nComparing this result to the options, it matches option H.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
