    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given the transfer function of a two port network H( \\omega ) = \\vertH(\\omega_0)\\vert exp(-j\\textphi). \\omega Derive an expression for output as a function of time, for the single frequency input v_i =cos\\omega_0t. \\omega\n\nOptions: \nA. |H(ω_0)|cos(2ω_0t - φ)\nB. \u000bertH(\\omega_0)\u000bertcos(\\omega_0t)\nC. |H(ω_0)|exp(-jω_0t)\nD. \u000bertH(\\omega_0)\u000bertcos(\\omega_0t - \textphi)\nE. \u000bertH(\\omega_0)\u000bertcos(\\omega_0t + \textphi)\nF. |H(ω_0)|exp(jω_0t)\nG. |H(ω_0)|sin(2ω_0t + φ)\nH. |H(ω_0)|sin(ω_0t - φ)\nI. |H(ω_0)|sin(ω_0t + φ)\nJ. \u000bertH(\\omega_0)\u000bertsin(\\omega_0t - \textphi)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the output of a linear time-invariant (LTI) system for a single frequency sinusoidal input, we multiply the input by the system's transfer function at that specific frequency.\n\n1.  **Input:** $v_i(t) = \\cos(\\omega_0 t)$. In phasor form, this is represented as $V_i = 1 \\angle 0^\\circ$.\n2.  **Transfer Function:** $H(\\omega_0) = |H(\\omega_0)| e^{-j\\phi}$, which means the system scales the amplitude by $|H(\\omega_0)|$ and shifts the phase by $-\\phi$.\n3.  **Output Phasor:** $V_o = V_i \\cdot H(\\omega_0) = 1 \\cdot |H(\\omega_0)| e^{-j\\phi} = |H(\\omega_0)| \\angle -\\phi$.\n4.  **Time Domain Conversion:** Converting the phasor back to the time domain gives $v_o(t) = |H(\\omega_0)| \\cos(\\omega_0 t - \\phi)$.\n\nDespite the character encoding errors in the options (where \"\u000bert\" appears to be a rendering error for vertical bars $|$), Option D matches this expression.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
