  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10872",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An input signal v(t) =I\\delta(t) (impulse function) is passed through a filter having function (1 - e-j\\omega\\tau)/j\\omegawhere \\tau is the stretchedumpulsewidth. Determine the output of the filter.\n\nOptions: \nA. v_o(t) = I [δ(t) * e^(-t/τ)]\nB. v_o(t) = I [e^(-jωt) - u(t - τ)]\nC. v_o(t) = I [1 - e^(-jωτ)]\nD. v_o(t) = I [u(t) / (u(t) + u(t - τ))]\nE. v_o(t) = I [u(t) / u(t - \tau)]\nF. v_o(t) = I [u(t) + u(t - \tau)]\nG. v_o(t) = I [u(t) * u(t - \tau)]\nH. v_o(t) = I [u(t) - u(t - \tau)]\nI. v_o(t) = I [δ(t) - e^(-t/τ)]\nJ. v_o(t) = I [sin(ωt) * u(t - τ)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the output of the filter, we use the property that the output $V_o(\\omega)$ in the frequency domain is the product of the input signal $V(\\omega)$ and the filter's transfer function $H(\\omega)$.\n\n1. The Fourier Transform of the input $v(t) = I\\delta(t)$ is $V(\\omega) = I$.\n2. The transfer function is $H(\\omega) = \\frac{1 - e^{-j\\omega\\tau}}{j\\omega}$.\n3. The output in the frequency domain is $V_o(\\omega) = I \\cdot \\frac{1 - e^{-j\\omega\\tau}}{j\\omega}$.\n4. Using the inverse Fourier Transform property $\\mathcal{F}^{-1}\\{ \\frac{1}{j\\omega} \\} = \\frac{1}{2} \\text{sgn}(t)$ (or more simply, the transform of a unit step $u(t)$ is $\\frac{1}{j\\omega} + \\pi\\delta(\\omega)$), the specific form $\\frac{1 - e^{-j\\omega\\tau}}{j\\omega}$ is the standard Fourier Transform of a rectangular pulse $p(t) = u(t) - u(t - \\tau)$.\n5. Thus, $v_o(t) = I[u(t) - u(t - \\tau)]$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
