  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10620",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A dc motor requires 10 kilowatts to enable it to supply its full capacity of 10 horsepower to its pulley. What is its full-load efficiency ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 74.6%\nB. 65%\nC. 50%\nD. 85%\nE. 92%\nF. 60%\nG. 80%\nH. 70%\nI. 90%\nJ. 78.2%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the full-load efficiency of the motor, we must compare the output power to the input power using the same units.\n\n1.  **Convert output power (hp) to kilowatts (kW):** \n    $1 \\text{ horsepower (hp)} = 0.746 \\text{ kilowatts (kW)}$\n    $\\text{Output Power} = 10 \\text{ hp} \\times 0.746 \\text{ kW/hp} = 7.46 \\text{ kW}$\n\n2.  **Calculate Efficiency ($\\eta$):**\n    $\\text{Efficiency} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Output Power}}{\\text{Input Power}} \\right) \\times 100$\n    $\\text{Efficiency} = \\left( \\frac{7.46 \\text{ kW}}{10 \\text{ kW}} \\right) \\times 100 = 74.6\\%$\n\nThe calculated efficiency matches Option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
