    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10465",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 7-hp motor takes 6.3 kilowatts at full load. What is its efficiency ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 75%\nB. 86%\nC. 95%\nD. 60%\nE. 80%\nF. 83%\nG. 65%\nH. 70%\nI. 78%\nJ. 90%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the efficiency of the motor, we first convert the output power from horsepower (hp) to kilowatts (kW). Using the conversion factor $1 \\text{ hp} = 0.746 \\text{ kW}$:\n$\\text{Output Power} = 7 \\text{ hp} \\times 0.746 \\text{ kW/hp} \\approx 5.222 \\text{ kW}$.\n\nEfficiency ($\\eta$) is the ratio of output power to input power:\n$\\eta = \\frac{\\text{Output Power}}{\\text{Input Power}} = \\frac{5.222 \\text{ kW}}{6.3 \\text{ kW}} \\approx 0.8288$ or $82.88\\%$.\n\nRounding to the nearest option provided, the efficiency is approximately 83%.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
