  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10914",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the ratio of reflected power to incident power, for a 75-ohm load on a 50-ohm line. Suppose a 50-ohm load is used instead of the 75-ohm load, what does it signify for an incident power of 50W?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 49W power to the load with 50 ohm\nB. 11 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 44.5W power to the load with 50 ohm\nC. 1 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 49.5W power to the load with 50 ohm\nD. 6 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 44W power to the load with 50 ohm\nE. 7 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 46.5W power to the load with 50 ohm\nF. 8 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 46W power to the load with 50 ohm\nG. 5 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 45W power to the load with 50 ohm\nH. 4 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies all the 50W power to the load with 50 ohm\nI. 3 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 47W power to the load with 50 ohm\nJ. 9 percent of the power is reflected; source supplies 45.5W power to the load with 50 ohm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the ratio of reflected power to incident power, we first calculate the reflection coefficient ($\\Gamma$) for a load $Z_L = 75\\ \\Omega$ on a characteristic impedance $Z_0 = 50\\ \\Omega$:\n$$\\Gamma = \\frac{Z_L - Z_0}{Z_L + Z_0} = \\frac{75 - 50}{75 + 50} = \\frac{25}{125} = 0.2$$\nThe ratio of reflected power to incident power is given by $|\\Gamma|^2$:\n$$\\text{Reflected Power Ratio} = (0.2)^2 = 0.04 = 4\\%$$\nFor the second part of the question, if a $50\\ \\Omega$ load is used on a $50\\ \\Omega$ line, the load is perfectly matched ($Z_L = Z_0$). In this case, the reflection coefficient $\\Gamma = 0$, meaning $0\\%$ of the power is reflected and all the incident power ($50\\text{W}$) is delivered to the load.\n\nComparing these results to the options, Option H matches both the 4% reflection for the 75-ohm load and the full power delivery for the 50-ohm load.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 417,
        "output_tokens": 286,
        "total_tokens": 703
