  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10474",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate the directivity of a short dipole.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 5\nC. 2.5\nD. 1\nE. 2\nF. 4\nG. 1.5\nH. 0.75\nI. 1.75\nJ. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The directivity ($D$) of a short dipole (also known as a Hertzian dipole) is a standard result in antenna theory. The radiation pattern of a short dipole is proportional to $\\sin^2\\theta$, and the integration of this pattern over a sphere results in a maximum directivity of 1.5. This means the short dipole concentrates energy more than an isotropic antenna, but less than a half-wave dipole (which has a directivity of 1.64).\n\n\\boxed{G}",
