    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10005",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A certain load to be driven at 1750 r/min requires a torque of 60 lb. ft. What horsepower will be required to drive the load ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15 hp\nB. 20 hp\nC. 10 hp\nD. 35 hp\nE. 5 hp\nF. 50 hp\nG. 30 hp\nH. 25 hp\nI. 40 hp\nJ. 45 hp\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the horsepower (hp) required to drive a load, the standard formula is:\n$\\text{hp} = \\frac{\\text{Torque (lb-ft)} \\times \\text{Speed (r/min)}}{5252}$\n\nPlugging in the given values:\n$\\text{hp} = \\frac{60 \\times 1750}{5252} = \\frac{105,000}{5252} \\approx 19.992$\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number gives 20 hp.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
