  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10061",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Methane reacts with water vapor at 25°C by the following reaction : CH_4(g) + H_2O(g) \\rightleftharpoons CO(g) + 3H_2(g) Using the following data, calculate the standard Gibbs free-energychange for this reaction. Data \\DeltaH_298^0(kcal mole^-1) \\DeltaS_298^0(cal deg^-1 mole^-1) CH_4(g) - 17.89 44.5 CO(g) - 26.40 47.3 H_2(g) 0 31.2 H_2O(g) - 57.80 45.1\n\nOptions: \nA. 34 kcal/mole\nB. 49,290 kcal/mole\nC. -10 kcal/mole\nD. 24.2 kcal/mole\nE. 60 kcal/mole\nF. 10,000 kcal/mole\nG. 15,280 kcal/mole\nH. 75.5 kcal/mole\nI. 51.3 kcal/mole\nJ. -20 kcal/mole\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the standard Gibbs free-energy change ($\\Delta G^\\circ$) for the reaction $\\text{CH}_4(g) + \\text{H}_2\\text{O}(g) \\rightleftharpoons \\text{CO}(g) + 3\\text{H}_2(g)$, we use the formula $\\Delta G^\\circ = \\Delta H^\\circ - T\\Delta S^\\circ$.\n\n1.  **Calculate $\\Delta H^\\circ$:**\n    $\\Delta H^\\circ = [\\Delta H_f^\\circ(\\text{CO}) + 3 \\times \\Delta H_f^\\circ(\\text{H}_2)] - [\\Delta H_f^\\circ(\\text{CH}_4) + \\Delta H_f^\\circ(\\text{H}_2\\text{O})]$\n    $\\Delta H^\\circ = [-26.40 + 3(0)] - [-17.89 + (-57.80)] = -26.40 - (-75.69) = 49.29 \\text{ kcal/mol}$\n\n2.  **Calculate $\\Delta S^\\circ$:**\n    $\\Delta S^\\circ = [S^\\circ(\\text{CO}) + 3 \\times S^\\circ(\\text{H}_2)] - [S^\\circ(\\text{CH}_4) + S^\\circ(\\text{H}_2\\text{O})]$\n    $\\Delta S^\\circ = [47.3 + 3(31.2)] - [44.5 + 45.1] = [47.3 + 93.6] - [89.6] = 140.9 - 89.6 = 51.3 \\text{ cal/K}\\cdot\\text{mol} = 0.0513 \\text{ kcal/K}\\cdot\\text{mol}$\n\n3.  **Calculate $\\Delta G^\\circ$ at $25^\\circ\\text{C}$ (298.15 K):**\n    $\\Delta G^\\circ = 49.29 \\text{ kcal/mol} - (298.15 \\text{ K} \\times 0.0513 \\text{ kcal/K}\\cdot\\text{mol}) \\approx 49.29 - 15.30 = 33.99 \\text{ kcal/mol}$\n\nThe result is approximately $34 \\text{ kcal/mol}$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
