  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10897",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The flow through a sluice gate set into a dam is to be investigated by building a model of the dam and sluice at 1 : 20 scale. Calculate the head at which the model should work to give conditions corresponding to a prototype head of 20 meters. If the discharge from the model under this corresponding head is 0.5 m^3/s, estimate the discharge from the prototype dam. A relationship between a set of physical variables can be stated as a relationship between a set of independent dimensionless groups made up from suitably chosen variables. The variables involved in this problem are Q -- the flow rate, d -- a leading dimension of the sluice, h -- the head over the sluice, \\rho -- the mass density of the water, g -- the gravity field intensity and \\mu -- the viscosity of water, so that there is some function, f (Q, \\rho, g, h, d, \\mu) = 0\n\nOptions: \nA. 1200 m^3/s\nB. 550 m^3/s\nC. 500 m^3/s\nD. 750 m^3/s\nE. 894 m^3/s\nF. 800 m^3/s\nG. 1000 m^3/s\nH. 425 m^3/s\nI. 650 m^3/s\nJ. 950 m^3/s\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we use the principles of hydraulic similarity. For a sluice gate where gravity is the dominant force (high Reynolds number), the flow is governed by Froude scaling.\n\n1.  **Head Calculation**: The ratio of heads is equal to the scale ratio $L_r$.\n    $h_m = h_p \\times (1/20) = 20\\text{ m} / 20 = 1\\text{ m}$.\n2.  **Discharge Calculation**: The discharge ratio $Q_r$ for Froude scaling is $L_r^{2.5}$.\n    $Q_p = Q_m / (L_r^{2.5}) = 0.5 / (1/20)^{2.5} = 0.5 \\times (20)^{2.5}$.\n    $20^{2.5} = 20^2 \\times \\sqrt{20} = 400 \\times 4.4721 \\approx 1788.85$.\n    $Q_p = 0.5 \\times 1788.85 = 894.425\\text{ m}^3/\\text{s}$.\n\nComparing this result to the options provided, the closest value is 894 $\\text{m}^3/\\text{s}$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
