      "generated_answer": "To determine if the resistor is voltage-controlled or current-controlled, we examine the provided characteristic equation: $v(t) = \\frac{1}{2}i^2(t)$.\n\n1.  In this equation, the voltage $v$ is expressed as a direct function of the current $i$.\n2.  By definition, if the voltage across a device is determined by the current flowing through it, the device is considered current-controlled.\n3.  While the relationship is nonlinear (square of the current), the controlling variable is the current.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
