      "generated_answer": "The theory of **antagonistic pleiotropy** suggests that senescence is an evolutionary byproduct of genes that offer a reproductive advantage early in life but have harmful effects later. One of the primary lines of evidence against this theory is the existence of organisms that exhibit **negligible senescence**, meaning they do not show a decline in survival probability or reproductive capability with age. While options I and D are similar, \"Some animals show little or no senescence\" is the standard empirical counter-argument cited in evolutionary biology literature.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{I}.",
