    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_5157",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What would be the frequency of AABBCC individuals from a mating of two AaBbCc individuals?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.0/4\nB. 1.0/512\nC. 1.0/1024\nD. 1.0/32\nE. 1.0/2\nF. 1.0/64\nG. 1.0/8\nH. 1.0/16\nI. 1.0/128\nJ. 1.0/256\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the frequency of the offspring AABBCC from a mating of two AaBbCc parents, we treat each gene pair as an independent Mendelian event.\n\n1. For each gene pair (e.g., Aa x Aa), the probability of getting a homozygous dominant offspring (AA) is $1/4$.\n2. Since there are three independent gene pairs (A, B, and C), we multiply the individual probabilities: $(1/4) \\times (1/4) \\times (1/4) = 1/64$.\n3. This result corresponds to the frequency of the specific genotype AABBCC.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
