    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_4861",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using this formula, if a reaction was provided with 84g of ethane and unlimited oxygen, how many grams of carbon dioxide would result (Carbon atomic weight: 12amu, Hydrogen atomic weight: 1amu, Oxygen atomic weight: 16amu)?\n﻿\nThe unbalanced reaction of ethane gas to carbon dioxide and water is as follows:\n\n C2H4 + O2 —> CO2 + H2O\n\nOptions: \nA. 78g\nB. 210g\nC. 312g\nD. 528g\nE. 156g\nF. 44g\nG. 264g\nH. 180g\nI. 132g\nJ. 396g\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this, first balance the chemical equation for the combustion of ethane (though the formula given $C_2H_4$ is actually ethylene, we will use the provided formula):\n$C_2H_4 + 3O_2 \\rightarrow 2CO_2 + 2H_2O$.\n\n1.  **Calculate Molar Masses:**\n    *   $C_2H_4$: $(2 \\times 12) + (4 \\times 1) = 28\\text{ g/mol}$\n    *   $CO_2$: $12 + (2 \\times 16) = 44\\text{ g/mol}$\n2.  **Calculate Moles of $C_2H_4$:**\n    *   $84\\text{g} / 28\\text{ g/mol} = 3\\text{ moles}$\n3.  **Calculate Mass of $CO_2$:**\n    *   From the balanced equation, 1 mole of $C_2H_4$ produces 2 moles of $CO_2$.\n    *   $3\\text{ moles } C_2H_4 \\times 2 = 6\\text{ moles } CO_2$.\n    *   $6\\text{ moles} \\times 44\\text{ g/mol} = 264\\text{g}$.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
