      "generated_answer": "When a peripheral motor nerve is severed, the muscles it innervates lose their trophic support and neural stimulation, leading to a significant decrease in muscle mass. After 6 months of denervation without regeneration, the most prominent and characteristic sign is the wasting away of the muscle tissue. Therefore, the muscles will show signs of significant atrophy.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
