      "generated_answer": "The p53 protein acts as a critical cell cycle checkpoint regulator that is activated by DNA damage, such as that caused by radiation. It primarily induces cell cycle arrest at the **G1** phase by stimulating the expression of p21, which inhibits cyclin-dependent kinases and prevents the transition to the S phase. A mutation in TP53 prevents this arrest, allowing cells with damaged DNA to continue proliferating.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{B}.",
