    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is determined by identifying the reinforcement schedules used: giving a sticker every day for being on time is a **continuous reinforcement schedule**, while giving a sticker for every three successful quizzes is a **fixed-ratio schedule** (specifically FR-3). In behavioral psychology, partial reinforcement schedules (like fixed-ratio) generally produce higher rates of response and more persistent behavior change than continuous reinforcement. Therefore, the students showed a stronger response to the fixed-ratio quiz reward than to the continuous daily attendance reward.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
