      "generated_answer": "The patient is a 15-year-old with Stage 2 hypertension (defined as $\\ge$ 95th percentile + 12 mmHg, or $\\ge$ 140/90 mmHg in adolescents) and a BMI at the 95th percentile (obesity). According to clinical guidelines for pediatric hypertension, initial management for Stage 2 hypertension, especially when associated with obesity, involves lifestyle modifications including weight loss and exercise. However, because she has persistent Stage 2 hypertension confirmed over multiple visits, the initiation of pharmacologic therapy is indicated alongside lifestyle changes, with ACE inhibitors like captopril being a first-line choice.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
