      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C**.\n\n\\boxed{C}\n\n**Explanation:** A feed-forward mechanism is an anticipatory response that prepares the body for a change before it actually occurs. Salivation on smelling food is a classic example because the digestive system prepares for food intake before the food even enters the mouth. Options A and B are examples of negative feedback mechanisms that respond to changes that have already occurred in the internal environment.",
