    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The concentration of a negative ion is 100 mMoUL extracellular and 10 mMo1/1 intracellular. What will be the Nernst potential for this ion?\n\nOptions: \nA. --10 mV\nB. +10 mV\nC. --61 mV\nD. +61 mV\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the Nernst potential ($E_{ion}$), we use the Nernst equation: $E_{ion} = \\frac{61}{z} \\log_{10} \\left( \\frac{[Ion]_{out}}{[Ion]_{in}} \\right)$.\n\n1.  **Identify the variables**: The ion is negative, so the valence $z = -1$. The extracellular concentration $[Ion]_{out}$ is $100\\text{ mM}$ and the intracellular concentration $[Ion]_{in}$ is $10\\text{ mM}$.\n2.  **Calculation**: $E_{ion} = \\frac{61}{-1} \\log_{10} \\left( \\frac{100}{10} \\right) = -61 \\times \\log_{10}(10) = -61 \\times 1 = -61\\text{ mV}$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
