    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A drug X was given continuous intravenous infusion at 1.6 mg/min. The clearance of the drug is 640 mL/min. With a half-life of 1.8 hours, what would be the steady state plasma concentration of drug?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.002 mg/mL\nB. 0.004 trig/mL\nC. 2.88 mg/mL\nD. 3.55 mg/mL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemma-4-31b-it",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the steady-state plasma concentration ($C_{ss}$), the formula is:\n$C_{ss} = \\frac{\\text{Infusion Rate (R)}}{\\text{Clearance (Cl)}}$\n\nFirst, ensure the units are compatible:\nInfusion Rate ($R$) = $1.6\\text{ mg/min}$\nClearance ($Cl$) = $640\\text{ mL/min}$\n\n$C_{ss} = \\frac{1.6\\text{ mg/min}}{640\\text{ mL/min}} = 0.0025\\text{ mg/mL}$\n\nLooking at the provided options, Option A (0.002 mg/mL) is the closest numerical value provided, though there is a slight discrepancy in the calculation result ($0.0025$ vs $0.002$). However, based on the magnitude of the other options, A is the only plausible answer.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
