    "prediction": "google/gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct sequence, we correlate the Jugular Venous Pulse (JVP) waves with the electrical and mechanical events of the cardiac cycle: the **\"a\" wave** (atrial contraction) follows the P wave and precedes the **R wave** (C), which is followed by the **First heart sound** (A) at the start of systole. This leads into the **Rapid ejection phase** (D), while the **T wave** (B) occurs later, signaling ventricular repolarization and coinciding with the \"v\" wave. Therefore, the sequence starting from the \"a\" wave is C $\\rightarrow$ A $\\rightarrow$ D $\\rightarrow$ B.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
