      "generated_answer": "The study found that routine laboratory parameters, specifically the Mean Corpuscular Volume (MCV), the AST/ALT ratio, and sex, were relevant regressors in distinguishing NASH from ASH with a high area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (aROC = 0.92). Notably, an elevated MCV was found in 53% of ASH patients but was normal in all NASH patients, and the AST/ALT ratio was also a significant predictor. Therefore, these routine markers are useful for differentiation.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
