      "generated_answer": "Based on the study results, the Glasgow Admission Prediction Score (GAPS) performed as well as or better than triage nurses. While nurses were accurate when they felt $\\ge$95% certain, GAPS significantly outperformed them in the majority of cases regarding calibration, discrimination, and accuracy. Therefore, the objective score is generally superior or at least comparable to nurse intuition.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
