      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct answer, we must first identify the notes of the **F Jue Ya-yue scale**. \n\n1.  **Identify the Tonic (Gong):** In a \"Jue\" mode scale, the name of the scale (F) refers to the **Jue** note. In the pentatonic system, Jue is a major third above Gong. If F is Jue, then the **Gong** note is **D♭** (or C♯).\n2.  **Identify the Scale Degrees:** The Ya-yue scale includes the five pentatonic notes plus **Bian Zhi** (augmented fourth from Gong) and **Bian Gong** (major seventh from Gong).\n    *   Gong = D♭\n    *   Bian Zhi = G (an augmented fourth above D♭)\n    *   Bian Gong = C (a major seventh above D♭)\n3.  **Analyze the Interval:** The relationship between **Bian Zhi (G)** and **Bian Gong (C)** is a perfect fourth (G to C). When expressed as a compound interval (adding an octave), it becomes a **perfect eleventh**.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
