      "generated_answer": "To determine the closely related keys of **D Shang mode**, we first identify its parent scale. D Shang belongs to the **C Major pentatonic system** (C Gong, D Shang, E Jue, G Zhi, A Yu). Closely related keys are those belonging to the same pentatonic system or those from systems with one sharp or one flat difference (F Major or G Major systems).\n\n1.  **C Zhi** belongs to the F Major system (F Gong).\n2.  **A Yu** belongs to the C Major system (Same as D Shang).\n3.  **F Jue** belongs to the C# Major system (or is not a standard member of the C, F, or G systems in this context).\n4.  **G Gong** belongs to the G Major system.\n\nIn traditional Chinese music theory, keys within the same system or adjacent systems (one accidental difference) are closely related; **F Jue** (belonging to the D-flat/C-sharp system) is the most distant.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
