      "generated_answer": "Based on the provided text, the specific reason for the women wearing masks is not explicitly stated, though the narrator notes that \"women will always go on trying to attract men\" even in a bleak future. The masks are described as sleek satin with gauze eyeholes, and the police officer mentions that \"rippers\" specifically target women to snag their skirts as a form of harassment. The context implies the coverings are a prevailing social fashion or protective custom in a dangerous, dystopian New York.\n\n\\boxed{The text does not explicitly state the origin of the custom, but implies the masks are a social fashion used while \"trying to attract men\" in a dangerous future where men known as \"rippers\" harass women by snagging their clothing.}",
